window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-01-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2"]={"id":"CGL-01-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2","title":"CGL 01 OCT 2026 SHIFT 2","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000072081","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Correct the equation by interchanging the two signs.<br>15 + 9 &#8722; 6 &#215; 3 &#247; 2 = 20 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो चिह्नों को परस्पर बदलकर समीकरण को सही कीजिए।<br>15 + 9 &#8722; 6 &#215; 3 &#247; 2 = 20 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"&#215; and &#247;","hi":"&#215; तथा &#247;"},"2":{"en":"+ and &#8722;","hi":"+ तथा &#8722;"},"3":{"en":"&#8722; and &#215;","hi":"&#8722; तथा &#215;"},"4":{"en":"&#247; and &#8722;","hi":"&#247; तथा &#8722;"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Interchanging &#215; with &#247; changes the equation to 15 + 9 &#8722; 6 &#247; 3 &#215; 2<br>6 &#247; 3 = 2 and 2 &#215; 2 = 4, so the value is 15 + 9 &#8722; 4 = 20 ✔<br>Other pairs give 15 &#8722; 9 + 6 &#215; 3 &#247; 2 = 15, 15 + 9 &#215; 6 &#8722; 3 &#247; 2 = 67.5 and 15 + 9 &#8722; 6 &#247; 3 &#215; 2 = 6, so none of them equals 20<br>Hence &#215; and &#247; must be interchanged<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): &#215; and &#247;.</b>","hi":"&#215; के स्थान पर &#247; रखने से समीकरण 15 + 9 &#8722; 6 &#247; 3 &#215; 2 बनता है<br>6 &#247; 3 = 2 तथा 2 &#215; 2 = 4, अतः मान 15 + 9 &#8722; 4 = 20 है ✔<br>अन्य युग्म 15 &#8722; 9 + 6 &#215; 3 &#247; 2 = 15, 15 + 9 &#215; 6 &#8722; 3 &#247; 2 = 67.5 तथा 15 + 9 &#8722; 6 &#247; 3 &#215; 2 = 6 देते हैं, अतः कोई भी 20 के बराबर नहीं है<br>इसलिए &#215; तथा &#247; परस्पर बदलने चाहिए<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): &#215; तथा &#247; है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000072082","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"Find the missing number: 8 : 28 :: 27 : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"लुप्त संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए: 8 : 28 :: 27 : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"63"},"2":{"en":"65"},"3":{"en":"67"},"4":{"en":"68"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The first number is a perfect cube: 8 = 2³, and the second number is the next cube plus one: 3³ + 1 = 28 ✔<br>Applying the same relation, 27 = 3³ and the next cube plus one is 4³ + 1 = 65<br>Hence the missing number is 65<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 65.</b>","hi":"पहली संख्या पूर्ण घन है: 8 = 2³, और दूसरी संख्या अगला घन जमा एक है: 3³ + 1 = 28 ✔<br>वही संबंध लगाने से 27 = 3³ तथा अगला घन जमा एक = 4³ + 1 = 65<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 65 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 65 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000072083","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"A man introduces a woman saying, \"She is the daughter of the only son of my father's wife.\" How is the woman related to the man? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक पुरुष एक महिला का परिचय देते हुए कहता है, \"वह मेरे पिता की पत्नी के एकमात्र पुत्र की पुत्री है।\" वह महिला उस पुरुष से किस प्रकार संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Daughter","hi":"पुत्री"},"2":{"en":"Sister","hi":"बहन"},"3":{"en":"Niece","hi":"भतीजी"},"4":{"en":"Cousin","hi":"चचेरी बहन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"My father's wife is my mother, and her only son is the man himself<br>So the woman is the daughter of the man<br>Hence she is his daughter<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Daughter.</b>","hi":"मेरे पिता की पत्नी मेरी माता है, और उसका एकमात्र पुत्र स्वयं वह पुरुष है<br>अतः वह महिला उस पुरुष की पुत्री है<br>इसलिए वह उसकी पुत्री है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): पुत्री है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000072084","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the question below three statements are given followed by four conclusions numbered I, II, III and IV. You must take the given statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the given statements, disregarding commonly known facts.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>All doctors attend conferences.<br>Some conference attendees are not experienced.<br>All experienced people lead research teams.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Some doctors are not experienced.<br>II. Some conference attendees lead research teams.<br>III. All experienced people attend conferences.<br>IV. Some research team leaders are not conference attendees. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"नीचे दिए प्रश्न में तीन कथन और उनके बाद I, II, III तथा IV क्रमांकित चार निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। दिए गए कथनों को सत्य मानना है, भले ही वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न प्रतीत हों, और फिर निर्णय कीजिए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-सा दिए गए कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है, सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों को उपेक्षित करते हुए।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सभी डॉक्टर सम्मेलनों में भाग लेते हैं।<br>कुछ सम्मेलन सहभागी अनुभवी नहीं हैं।<br>सभी अनुभवी लोग शोध दलों का नेतृत्व करते हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कुछ डॉक्टर अनुभवी नहीं हैं।<br>II. कुछ सम्मेलन सहभागी शोध दलों का नेतृत्व करते हैं।<br>III. सभी अनुभवी लोग सम्मेलनों में भाग लेते हैं।<br>IV. कुछ शोध दल नेतृत्वकर्ता सम्मेलन सहभागी नहीं हैं। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I and II follow","hi":"केवल I और II निकलते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only III follows","hi":"केवल III निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Only II and III follow","hi":"केवल II और III निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"None follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"All doctors attend conferences, but nothing says which conference attendees are the inexperienced ones, so we cannot say that some doctors are not experienced, and conclusion I does not follow<br>Some attendees are not experienced, and only the experienced attendees are known to lead research teams, so no attendee is proved to lead a team and conclusion II does not follow<br>All experienced people lead research teams, which says nothing about attending conferences, so conclusion III does not follow<br>The statement does not connect research team leaders with non-attendees, so conclusion IV does not follow<br>Hence none of the conclusions follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): None follows.</b>","hi":"सभी डॉक्टर सम्मेलनों में भाग लेते हैं, परंतु यह नहीं कहा गया कि कौन-से सहभागी अनुभवी नहीं हैं, अतः यह नहीं कह सकते कि कुछ डॉक्टर अनुभवी नहीं हैं, और निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता<br>कुछ सहभागी अनुभवी नहीं हैं, और केवल अनुभवी सहभागी ही शोध दलों का नेतृत्व करते हैं, अतः किसी सहभागी का नेतृत्व सिद्ध नहीं होता और निष्कर्ष II नहीं निकलता<br>सभी अनुभवी लोग शोध दलों का नेतृत्व करते हैं, जिससे सम्मेलन में भाग लेने की कोई बात नहीं निकलती, अतः निष्कर्ष III नहीं निकलता<br>कथन शोध दल नेतृत्वकर्ताओं को गैर-सहभागियों से नहीं जोड़ता, अतः निष्कर्ष IV नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए कोई भी निष्कर्ष नहीं निकलता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): कोई नहीं निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000072085","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Which of the following numbers will replace the question mark (?) in the given series?<br>1, 9, 65, 457, ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी संख्या दी गई श्रेणी में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर आएगी?<br>1, 9, 65, 457, ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3125"},"2":{"en":"3201"},"3":{"en":"3850"},"4":{"en":"4265"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The differences between the consecutive terms are 8, 56 and 392<br>Each difference is seven times the difference before it: 8 × 7 = 56 and 56 × 7 = 392 ✔<br>So the next difference is 392 × 7 = 2744, and the next term is 457 + 2744 = 3201<br>Hence the missing number is 3201<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3201.</b>","hi":"क्रमागत पदों के अंतर 8, 56 तथा 392 हैं<br>प्रत्येक अंतर अपने पहले के अंतर का सात गुना है: 8 × 7 = 56 तथा 56 × 7 = 392 ✔<br>अतः अगला अंतर 392 × 7 = 2744 है और अगला पद 457 + 2744 = 3201 है<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 3201 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3201 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000072086","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"How many letters will remain at the same position in the word 'PRINTER' when arranged alphabetically? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"शब्द 'PRINTER' को वर्णमाला के क्रम में व्यवस्थित करने पर कितने अक्षर अपने स्थान पर ही रहेंगे? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"PRINTER has the letters P, R, I, N, T, E and R, whose alphabetical order is E, I, N, P, R, T<br>Comparing place by place, P→E, R→I, I→N, N→P, T→R, E→R and R→T, so no letter keeps its old place<br>Hence 0 letters remain at the same position<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 0.</b>","hi":"PRINTER में अक्षर P, R, I, N, T, E तथा R हैं, जिनका वर्णमाला क्रम E, I, N, P, R, T है<br>स्थान-दर-स्थान तुलना करने पर P→E, R→I, I→N, N→P, T→R, E→R तथा R→T, अतः कोई अक्षर अपने पुराने स्थान पर नहीं रहता<br>इसलिए 0 अक्षर अपने स्थान पर रहते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000072087","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। यह पैटर्न पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In every column the bottom number is the product of the first two numbers divided by the third number<br>First column: 5 × 6 ÷ 2 = 15 ✔ and second column: 4 × 7 ÷ 2 = 14 ✔<br>Third column: 3 × 2 ÷ ? = 6, so ? = 6 ÷ 6 = 1<br>Hence the missing number is 1<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक स्तंभ में नीचे की संख्या पहली दो संख्याओं के गुणनफल को तीसरी संख्या से भाग देने पर मिलती है<br>पहला स्तंभ: 5 × 6 ÷ 2 = 15 ✔ तथा दूसरा स्तंभ: 4 × 7 ÷ 2 = 14 ✔<br>तीसरा स्तंभ: 3 × 2 ÷ ? = 6, अतः ? = 6 ÷ 6 = 1<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 1 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000072088","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"Read the following information carefully and answer the question that follows.<br>1. A + B means \"A is the brother of B\"<br>2. A * B means \"A is the father of B\"<br>3. A / B means \"A is the mother of B\"<br>Which of the following expressions correctly represents the relationship that P is the son of S? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित जानकारी ध्यान से पढ़िए और आगे दिए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br>1. A + B का अर्थ है \"A, B का भाई है\"<br>2. A * B का अर्थ है \"A, B का पिता है\"<br>3. A / B का अर्थ है \"A, B की माता है\"<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा व्यंजक इस संबंध को सही दर्शाता है कि P, S का पुत्र है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"P + Q * S"},"2":{"en":"P * Q / S"},"3":{"en":"P + Q / S"},"4":{"en":"S * P + Q"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In S * P + Q the expression S * P means S is the father of P, so P is a child of S<br>P + Q means P is the brother of Q, which shows that P is male<br>Together they mean that P is the son of S ✔<br>The other options make P the brother, the father or the mother of S, which does not give the required relation<br>Hence S * P + Q is the correct expression<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): S * P + Q.</b>","hi":"S * P + Q में S * P का अर्थ है S, P का पिता है, अतः P, S की संतान है<br>P + Q का अर्थ है P, Q का भाई है, जिससे स्पष्ट है कि P पुरुष है<br>दोनों मिलकर अर्थ देते हैं कि P, S का पुत्र है ✔<br>अन्य विकल्प P को S का भाई, पिता या माता बनाते हैं, जिससे आवश्यक संबंध नहीं मिलता<br>इसलिए S * P + Q सही व्यंजक है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): S * P + Q है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000072089","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"Read the following instructions and answer the question that follows:<br>1. A + B, then A is the brother of B.<br>2. A % B, then A is the son of B.<br>3. A &amp; B, then A is the wife of B.<br>4. A = B, then A is the husband of B.<br>5. A @ B, then A is the daughter of B.<br>If C &amp; D + E @ F = G @ H, then which of the following options is <b>not</b> correct? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित निर्देश पढ़िए और आगे दिए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br>1. A + B, तो A, B का भाई है।<br>2. A % B, तो A, B का पुत्र है।<br>3. A &amp; B, तो A, B की पत्नी है।<br>4. A = B, तो A, B का पति है।<br>5. A @ B, तो A, B की पुत्री है।<br>यदि C &amp; D + E @ F = G @ H है, तो निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प <b>सही नहीं</b> है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"E is the granddaughter of H.","hi":"E, H की पौत्री है।"},"2":{"en":"C is the daughter-in-law of F.","hi":"C, F की पुत्रवधू है।"},"3":{"en":"F is the mother of E.","hi":"F, E की माता है।"},"4":{"en":"D is the son of G.","hi":"D, G का पुत्र है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"C &amp; D makes C the wife of D, and D + E makes D the brother of E<br>E @ F makes E the daughter of F, and F = G makes F the husband of G, so F is male<br>G @ H makes G the daughter of H<br>So E is the daughter of F and G and the granddaughter of H ✔, C is the wife of D and hence the daughter-in-law of F ✔, and D is the brother of E and hence the son of G ✔<br>Since F is the husband of G and is male, F cannot be the mother of E, so that statement is not correct<br>Hence F is the mother of E is the incorrect option<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): F is the mother of E..</b>","hi":"C &amp; D से C, D की पत्नी है, और D + E से D, E का भाई है<br>E @ F से E, F की पुत्री है, और F = G से F, G का पति है, अतः F पुरुष है<br>G @ H से G, H की पुत्री है<br>अतः E, F और G की पुत्री तथा H की पौत्री है ✔, C, D की पत्नी और इसलिए F की पुत्रवधू है ✔, तथा D, E का भाई और इसलिए G का पुत्र है ✔<br>चूँकि F, G का पति है और पुरुष है, F, E की माता नहीं हो सकता, अतः वह कथन सही नहीं है<br>इसलिए 'F, E की माता है' गलत विकल्प है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): F, E की माता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000072090","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">27</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। यह पैटर्न पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">27</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8"},"2":{"en":"12"},"3":{"en":"4"},"4":{"en":"16"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In every row the product of the first and the third numbers is 8: 2 × 4 = 8 ✔, 4 × 2 = 8 ✔, 8 × 1 = 8 ✔ and 4 × 2 = 8 ✔<br>So for the last row ? × 2 = 8, which gives ? = 4<br>The middle column follows its own pattern of 3, 9, 27 and 9, which does not affect the missing entry<br>Hence the missing number is 4<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 4.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में पहली तथा तीसरी संख्या का गुणनफल 8 है: 2 × 4 = 8 ✔, 4 × 2 = 8 ✔, 8 × 1 = 8 ✔ तथा 4 × 2 = 8 ✔<br>अतः अंतिम पंक्ति के लिए ? × 2 = 8, जिससे ? = 4<br>मध्य स्तंभ 3, 9, 27 तथा 9 के अपने पैटर्न का पालन करता है, जो लुप्त पद को प्रभावित नहीं करता<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 4 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000072091","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"In a secure database, roll numbers follow the format: [Digit A] [Digit B] [Digit C] where A &#215; C = B + 2. Which of the following roll number is invalid? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक सुरक्षित डेटाबेस में रोल नंबर का प्रारूप [अंक A] [अंक B] [अंक C] है, जहाँ A &#215; C = B + 2 है। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा रोल नंबर अमान्य है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"373"},"2":{"en":"462"},"3":{"en":"582"},"4":{"en":"6112"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"For 373, A × C = 3 × 3 = 9 and B + 2 = 7 + 2 = 9 ✔<br>For 462, 4 × 2 = 8 and 6 + 2 = 8 ✔, and for 582, 5 × 2 = 10 and 8 + 2 = 10 ✔<br>For 6112 the middle digit is 11, which is not a single digit, so the format itself fails ✘<br>Hence 6112 is the invalid roll number<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 6112.</b>","hi":"373 के लिए A × C = 3 × 3 = 9 तथा B + 2 = 7 + 2 = 9 ✔<br>462 के लिए 4 × 2 = 8 तथा 6 + 2 = 8 ✔, और 582 के लिए 5 × 2 = 10 तथा 8 + 2 = 10 ✔<br>6112 में मध्य अंक 11 है, जो एक अंक नहीं है, अतः प्रारूप ही विफल हो जाता है ✘<br>इसलिए 6112 अमान्य रोल नंबर है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 6112 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000072092","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>KAN, OZR, SYV, ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न जाँचिए और श्रेणी में अगला अक्षर-समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>KAN, OZR, SYV, ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"WXZ"},"2":{"en":"WYZ"},"3":{"en":"WWY"},"4":{"en":"WXY"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The first letters K, O, S move four places ahead each time, so the next first letter is W<br>The second letters A, Z, Y move one place back each time, so after Y the next second letter is X<br>The third letters N, R, V move four places ahead each time, so the next third letter is Z<br>Hence the next set of letters is WXZ<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): WXZ.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर K, O, S प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला पहला अक्षर W है<br>दूसरे अक्षर A, Z, Y प्रत्येक बार एक स्थान पीछे जाते हैं, अतः Y के बाद अगला दूसरा अक्षर X है<br>तीसरे अक्षर N, R, V प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला तीसरा अक्षर Z है<br>इसलिए अगला अक्षर-समूह WXZ है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): WXZ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000072093","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Select the odd number pair from the given alternatives. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से विषम संख्या-युग्म चुनिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25, 650"},"2":{"en":"16, 272"},"3":{"en":"13, 186"},"4":{"en":"20, 420"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In the first, second and fourth pairs the second number is the first number multiplied by the number next to it: 25 × 26 = 650 ✔, 16 × 17 = 272 ✔ and 20 × 21 = 420 ✔<br>For the third pair 13 × 14 = 182, not 186 ✘<br>Hence 13, 186 is the odd pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 13, 186.</b>","hi":"पहले, दूसरे तथा चौथे युग्म में दूसरी संख्या पहली संख्या को उसके अगली संख्या से गुणा करने पर मिलती है: 25 × 26 = 650 ✔, 16 × 17 = 272 ✔ तथा 20 × 21 = 420 ✔<br>तीसरे युग्म के लिए 13 × 14 = 182 है, 186 नहीं ✘<br>इसलिए 13, 186 विषम युग्म है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 13, 186 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000072094","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Read the question carefully and choose the most appropriate option.<br>You are managing a community cleanliness drive. Participation is lower than expected because many residents believe the effort will not make a difference. What would you do? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़िए और सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br>आप एक सामुदायिक स्वच्छता अभियान का प्रबंधन कर रहे हैं। भागीदारी अपेक्षा से कम है क्योंकि अनेक निवासियों का मानना है कि इस प्रयास से कोई अंतर नहीं पड़ेगा। आप क्या करेंगे? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Criticize the residents publicly for not supporting the initiative.","hi":"पहल का समर्थन न करने के लिए निवासियों की सार्वजनिक रूप से आलोचना करना।"},"2":{"en":"Cancel the drive because community participation is currently low.","hi":"समुदाय की भागीदारी कम होने के कारण अभियान रद्द कर देना।"},"3":{"en":"Continue silently without trying to involve additional community members.","hi":"अतिरिक्त समुदाय सदस्यों को शामिल करने का प्रयास किए बिना चुपचाप जारी रखना।"},"4":{"en":"Engage residents positively and explain the benefits of participation.","hi":"निवासियों से सकारात्मक रूप से जुड़ना और भागीदारी के लाभ समझाना।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The low turnout comes from a belief that the effort will not help, so the answer is to remove that belief<br>Engaging residents positively and explaining the benefits of participation gives them a reason to join and keeps the drive alive<br>Criticising them pushes them further away, cancelling the drive loses everything, and continuing silently leaves the doubt untouched<br>Hence engaging residents positively and explaining the benefits of participation is the right action<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Engage residents positively and explain the benefits of participation..</b>","hi":"कम भागीदारी इस विश्वास से है कि प्रयास से लाभ नहीं होगा, अतः उपाय यह विश्वास दूर करना है<br>निवासियों से सकारात्मक रूप से जुड़ना और भागीदारी के लाभ समझाना उन्हें जुड़ने का कारण देता है और अभियान जीवित रखता है<br>आलोचना उन्हें और दूर करती है, अभियान रद्द करने से सब कुछ चला जाता है, और चुपचाप जारी रखने से संदेह बना रहता है<br>अतः निवासियों से सकारात्मक रूप से जुड़ना और भागीदारी के लाभ समझाना सही कार्य है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): निवासियों से सकारात्मक रूप से जुड़ना और भागीदारी के लाभ समझाना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000072095","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br>G7M : N14T :: U21A : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>G7M : N14T :: U21A : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"B28H"},"2":{"en":"C28H"},"3":{"en":"B27H"},"4":{"en":"B28G"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In G7M : N14T each letter moves seven places ahead (G→N and M→T) and the number grows by seven (7 → 14)<br>Applying the same steps to U21A: U + 7 = B, 21 + 7 = 28 and A + 7 = H<br>Hence the answer is B28H<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): B28H.</b>","hi":"G7M : N14T में प्रत्येक अक्षर सात स्थान आगे जाता है (G→N तथा M→T) और संख्या सात बढ़ती है (7 → 14)<br>U21A पर वही चरण लगाने से U + 7 = B, 21 + 7 = 28 तथा A + 7 = H<br>इसलिए उत्तर B28H है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): B28H है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000072096","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the given question, a few statements have been given followed by conclusions based on them. Consider the statements to be true and answer which of the given conclusions logically follow the statement.<br><b>Statements</b><br>1. All architects are planners.<br>2. All planners are visionaries.<br>3. No visionary is impractical.<br><b>Conclusions</b><br>I. All architects are visionaries.<br>II. No architect is impractical.<br>III. Some visionaries are architects.<br>IV. No planner is impractical. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए प्रश्न में कुछ कथन और उनके आधार पर निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए और उत्तर दीजिए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-से कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन</b><br>1. सभी वास्तुकार योजनाकार हैं।<br>2. सभी योजनाकार दूरदर्शी हैं।<br>3. कोई दूरदर्शी अव्यावहारिक नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष</b><br>I. सभी वास्तुकार दूरदर्शी हैं।<br>II. कोई वास्तुकार अव्यावहारिक नहीं है।<br>III. कुछ दूरदर्शी वास्तुकार हैं।<br>IV. कोई योजनाकार अव्यावहारिक नहीं है। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I, II and IV follow","hi":"केवल I, II और IV निकलते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only I and III follow","hi":"केवल I और III निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"All four follow","hi":"चारों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only II and III follow","hi":"केवल II और III निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"All architects are planners and all planners are visionaries, so all architects are visionaries and conclusion I follows ✔<br>Since no visionary is impractical and every architect is a visionary, no architect can be impractical, so conclusion II follows ✔<br>Architects exist and all of them are visionaries, so some visionaries are architects and conclusion III follows ✔<br>All planners are visionaries and no visionary is impractical, so no planner is impractical and conclusion IV follows ✔<br>Hence all four conclusions follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): All four follow.</b>","hi":"सभी वास्तुकार योजनाकार हैं और सभी योजनाकार दूरदर्शी हैं, अतः सभी वास्तुकार दूरदर्शी हैं और निष्कर्ष I निकलता है ✔<br>चूँकि कोई दूरदर्शी अव्यावहारिक नहीं है और प्रत्येक वास्तुकार दूरदर्शी है, अतः कोई वास्तुकार अव्यावहारिक नहीं हो सकता और निष्कर्ष II निकलता है ✔<br>वास्तुकार होते हैं और वे सभी दूरदर्शी हैं, अतः कुछ दूरदर्शी वास्तुकार हैं और निष्कर्ष III निकलता है ✔<br>सभी योजनाकार दूरदर्शी हैं और कोई दूरदर्शी अव्यावहारिक नहीं है, अतः कोई योजनाकार अव्यावहारिक नहीं है और निष्कर्ष IV निकलता है ✔<br>इसलिए चारों निष्कर्ष निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): चारों निकलते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000072097","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the given question, a few statements have been given followed by conclusions based on them. Consider the statements to be true and answer which of the given conclusions logically follow the statement.<br><b>Statements</b><br>1. No antibiotic is harmless.<br>2. Some medicines are antibiotics.<br>3. All prescribed drugs are medicines.<br><b>Conclusions</b><br>I. Some medicines are not harmless.<br>II. No prescribed drug is harmless.<br>III. Some prescribed drugs are antibiotics.<br>IV. Some antibiotics are prescribed drugs. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए प्रश्न में कुछ कथन और उनके आधार पर निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए और उत्तर दीजिए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-से कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन</b><br>1. कोई एंटीबायोटिक हानिरहित नहीं है।<br>2. कुछ दवाइयाँ एंटीबायोटिक हैं।<br>3. सभी निर्धारित औषधियाँ दवाइयाँ हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष</b><br>I. कुछ दवाइयाँ हानिरहित नहीं हैं।<br>II. कोई निर्धारित औषधि हानिरहित नहीं है।<br>III. कुछ निर्धारित औषधियाँ एंटीबायोटिक हैं।<br>IV. कुछ एंटीबायोटिक निर्धारित औषधियाँ हैं। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I, III and IV follow","hi":"केवल I, III और IV निकलते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only I and III follow","hi":"केवल I और III निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Only I and IV follow","hi":"केवल I और IV निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Some medicines are antibiotics and no antibiotic is harmless, so those medicines are not harmless, which makes conclusion I follow ✔<br>Prescribed drugs are medicines, but nothing says that any prescribed drug is an antibiotic, so conclusions II, III and IV are not definite ✘<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only I follows.</b>","hi":"कुछ दवाइयाँ एंटीबायोटिक हैं और कोई एंटीबायोटिक हानिरहित नहीं है, अतः वे दवाइयाँ हानिरहित नहीं हैं और निष्कर्ष I निकलता है ✔<br>निर्धारित औषधियाँ दवाइयाँ हैं, परंतु यह नहीं कहा गया कि कोई निर्धारित औषधि एंटीबायोटिक है, अतः निष्कर्ष II, III तथा IV निश्चित नहीं हैं ✘<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000072098","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Which two signs should be interchanged to make the equation below mathematically correct?<br>16 &#8722; 8 &#247; 4 + 5 &#215; 2 = 8 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"नीचे दिए समीकरण को गणितीय रूप से सही बनाने के लिए किन दो चिह्नों को परस्पर बदलना चाहिए?<br>16 &#8722; 8 &#247; 4 + 5 &#215; 2 = 8 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"&#247; and &#215;","hi":"&#247; तथा &#215;"},"2":{"en":"&#8722; and +","hi":"&#8722; तथा +"},"3":{"en":"&#215; and &#8722;","hi":"&#215; तथा &#8722;"},"4":{"en":"&#247; and +","hi":"&#247; तथा +"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Interchanging &#8722; with + changes the equation to 16 + 8 &#247; 4 &#8722; 5 &#215; 2<br>8 &#247; 4 = 2 and 5 &#215; 2 = 10, so the value is 16 + 2 &#8722; 10 = 8 ✔<br>The other pairs give 16 &#8722; 8 &#215; 4 + 5 &#247; 2 = &#8722;13.5, 16 &#215; 8 &#247; 4 + 5 &#8722; 2 = 35 and 16 &#8722; 8 + 4 &#247; 5 &#215; 2 = 9.6, so none of them equals 8<br>Hence &#8722; and + must be interchanged<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): &#8722; and +.</b>","hi":"&#8722; के स्थान पर + रखने से समीकरण 16 + 8 &#247; 4 &#8722; 5 &#215; 2 बनता है<br>8 &#247; 4 = 2 तथा 5 &#215; 2 = 10, अतः मान 16 + 2 &#8722; 10 = 8 है ✔<br>अन्य युग्म 16 &#8722; 8 &#215; 4 + 5 &#247; 2 = &#8722;13.5, 16 &#215; 8 &#247; 4 + 5 &#8722; 2 = 35 तथा 16 &#8722; 8 + 4 &#247; 5 &#215; 2 = 9.6 देते हैं, अतः कोई भी 8 के बराबर नहीं है<br>इसलिए &#8722; तथा + परस्पर बदलने चाहिए<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): &#8722; तथा + है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000072099","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>In a T-20 cricket match, the total wickets taken by a team were 9. Out of these, 6 wickets were taken by spinners.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. 80% of the bowlers in the team were spinners.<br>II. The opening bowlers of the team were spinners. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक टी-20 क्रिकेट मैच में एक टीम ने कुल 9 विकेट लिए। इनमें से 6 विकेट स्पिनरों ने लिए।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. टीम के 80% गेंदबाज़ स्पिनर थे।<br>II. टीम के शुरुआती गेंदबाज़ स्पिनर थे। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The statement speaks about the wickets taken, not about how many bowlers bowled, so the figure 80% has no basis and conclusion I does not follow<br>Nothing is said about who opened the bowling, so conclusion II does not follow either<br>Hence neither conclusion I nor II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Neither conclusion I nor II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन लिए गए विकेटों की बात करता है, यह नहीं कि कितने गेंदबाज़ गेंदबाज़ी कर रहे थे, अतः 80% का कोई आधार नहीं और निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता<br>यह भी नहीं कहा गया कि शुरुआती गेंदबाज़ी किसने की, अतः निष्कर्ष II भी नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000072100","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"In the following question a statement is given followed by some assumptions. Read the assumptions carefully and choose the appropriate option.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A transport company is launching a new fleet of electric buses and promoting the service extensively. To finance the project, it plans to reduce non-essential expenses and obtain funding from financial institutions.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. The new electric bus service is likely to attract passengers.<br>II. Financial institutions will surely provide the required funding. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ अवधारणाएँ दी गई हैं। अवधारणाएँ ध्यान से पढ़िए और उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक परिवहन कंपनी इलेक्ट्रिक बसों का नया बेड़ा शुरू कर रही है और सेवा का व्यापक प्रचार कर रही है। परियोजना के वित्तपोषण के लिए वह गैर-आवश्यक व्यय घटाने तथा वित्तीय संस्थानों से धन प्राप्त करने की योजना बना रही है।<br><b>अवधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. नई इलेक्ट्रिक बस सेवा के यात्रियों को आकर्षित करने की संभावना है।<br>II. वित्तीय संस्थान आवश्यक धन निश्चित रूप से प्रदान करेंगे। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I is implicit.","hi":"केवल I निहित है।"},"2":{"en":"Only II is implicit.","hi":"केवल II निहित है।"},"3":{"en":"Neither I nor II is implicit.","hi":"न तो I और न ही II निहित है।"},"4":{"en":"Both I and II are implicit.","hi":"I और II दोनों निहित हैं।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A company spends on extensive promotion only when it expects the service to attract passengers, so assumption I is implicit ✔<br>Planning to obtain funding is not the same as assuming that the funding will surely come, so the word surely makes assumption II too strong ✘<br>Hence only I is implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I is implicit..</b>","hi":"कंपनी व्यापक प्रचार पर व्यय तभी करती है जब उसे आशा हो कि सेवा यात्रियों को आकर्षित करेगी, अतः अवधारणा I निहित है ✔<br>धन प्राप्त करने की योजना बनाना यह मान लेना नहीं है कि धन निश्चित रूप से मिल जाएगा, अतः 'निश्चित रूप से' शब्द अवधारणा II को अत्यधिक बना देता है ✘<br>इसलिए केवल I निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I निहित है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000072101","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"What government action yields the highest increase in crop productivity in areas where traditional farming techniques predominate? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"जिन क्षेत्रों में पारंपरिक खेती तकनीकें प्रमुख हैं, वहाँ कौन-सी सरकारी कार्यवाही फसल उत्पादकता में सर्वाधिक वृद्धि देती है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Provide annual total debt waivers.","hi":"प्रतिवर्ष पूर्ण ऋण माफ़ी प्रदान करना।"},"2":{"en":"Implement smart precision farming systems.","hi":"स्मार्ट सटीक खेती प्रणालियाँ लागू करना।"},"3":{"en":"Cease all agricultural product exports.","hi":"सभी कृषि उत्पादों का निर्यात बंद करना।"},"4":{"en":"Import more foreign farming goods.","hi":"अधिक विदेशी कृषि वस्तुओं का आयात करना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Productivity rises when farmers use better inputs, better seeds and better methods on the same land<br>Smart precision farming systems bring exactly this improvement in water, fertiliser and sowing, so they raise output per hectare ✔<br>Debt waivers give relief but do not raise output, stopping exports does not affect yield and importing goods does not help local farms at all<br>Hence implementing smart precision farming systems gives the highest increase in crop productivity<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Implement smart precision farming systems..</b>","hi":"उत्पादकता तब बढ़ती है जब किसान उसी भूमि पर बेहतर आदान, बेहतर बीज तथा बेहतर विधियाँ अपनाएँ<br>स्मार्ट सटीक खेती प्रणालियाँ जल, उर्वरक तथा बुवाई में ठीक यही सुधार लाती हैं, अतः प्रति हेक्टेयर उत्पादन बढ़ता है ✔<br>ऋण माफ़ी राहत देती है परंतु उत्पादन नहीं बढ़ाती, निर्यात रोकने से उपज पर असर नहीं पड़ता और वस्तुओं का आयात स्थानीय खेतों की सहायता नहीं करता<br>अतः स्मार्ट सटीक खेती प्रणालियाँ लागू करना फसल उत्पादकता में सर्वाधिक वृद्धि देता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): स्मार्ट सटीक खेती प्रणालियाँ लागू करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000072102","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word.<br>Clove : Flower bud :: Cinnamon : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है।<br>Clove : Flower bud :: Cinnamon : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Stem","hi":"तना"},"2":{"en":"Bark","hi":"छाल"},"3":{"en":"Root","hi":"जड़"},"4":{"en":"Seed","hi":"बीज"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A clove is the dried flower bud of a plant<br>In the same way cinnamon is the dried inner bark of the cinnamon tree ✔<br>Stem, root and seed are other plant parts but they are not what cinnamon is<br>Hence the answer is Bark<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Bark.</b>","hi":"Clove पौधे की सुखाई गई पुष्प कली है<br>उसी प्रकार Cinnamon दालचीनी के वृक्ष की सुखाई गई भीतरी छाल है ✔<br>तना, जड़ तथा बीज पौधे के अन्य भाग हैं, परंतु दालचीनी इनमें से नहीं है<br>इसलिए उत्तर Bark है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): छाल है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000072103","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a specific casing code, the letter K is written in lowercase. All letters appearing before K in the alphabet are written in uppercase, while all letters from K onwards alternate between lowercase and uppercase (i.e., ..., I, j, k, L, m, N...). Under this rule, how will the word 'MONDAY' be written? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक विशिष्ट केसिंग कूट में K अक्षर छोटे अक्षर में लिखा जाता है। वर्णमाला में K से पहले आने वाले सभी अक्षर बड़े अक्षरों में लिखे जाते हैं, जबकि K से आगे के सभी अक्षर छोटे और बड़े अक्षरों के बीच बदलते हैं (अर्थात् ..., I, j, k, L, m, N...)। इस नियम के अनुसार शब्द 'MONDAY' कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"MoNdAy"},"2":{"en":"mOnDaY"},"3":{"en":"moNDAY"},"4":{"en":"MoNdAY"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"From K onwards the letters alternate between lowercase and uppercase, starting with k in lowercase: k small, L capital, m small, N capital, o small, P capital, q small, R capital, s small, T capital, u small, V capital, w small, X capital and y small<br>Reading MONDAY under this rule: M(13) is small = m, O(15) is small = o, N(14) is capital = N, D(4) is capital = D, A(1) is capital = A and Y(25) is capital = Y<br>Hence MONDAY is written as moNDAY<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): moNDAY.</b>","hi":"K से आगे अक्षर k छोटे से शुरू करके छोटे और बड़े के बीच बदलते हैं: k छोटा, L बड़ा, m छोटा, N बड़ा, o छोटा, P बड़ा, q छोटा, R बड़ा, s छोटा, T बड़ा, u छोटा, V बड़ा, w छोटा, X बड़ा तथा y छोटा<br>इस नियम से MONDAY पढ़ने पर M(13) छोटा = m, O(15) छोटा = o, N(14) बड़ा = N, D(4) बड़ा = D, A(1) बड़ा = A तथा Y(25) बड़ा = Y<br>इसलिए MONDAY को moNDAY लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): moNDAY है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000072104","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"Direction: Choose the most logical course of action.<br><b>Scenario:</b><br>A company saves 15% by using Supplier X, but Supplier X's defect rate recently rose from 1% to 5%, causing production delays. Alternative suppliers are highly reliable but charge standard market rates. The company operates on tight profit margins and strict delivery schedules.<br>What is the most appropriate action? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निर्देश: सर्वाधिक तार्किक कार्यवाही चुनिए।<br><b>परिदृश्य:</b><br>एक कंपनी Supplier X का उपयोग करके 15% बचत करती है, परंतु Supplier X की खराबी दर हाल ही में 1% से बढ़कर 5% हो गई है, जिससे उत्पादन में देरी हो रही है। वैकल्पिक आपूर्तिकर्ता अत्यधिक विश्वसनीय हैं परंतु मानक बाज़ार दरें लेते हैं। कंपनी कम लाभ मार्जिन तथा कड़े डिलीवरी कार्यक्रम पर चलती है।<br>सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त कार्यवाही क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Shift 100% of procurement to alternative suppliers immediately to eliminate defects.","hi":"खराबी समाप्त करने के लिए तुरंत 100% खरीद वैकल्पिक आपूर्तिकर्ताओं को स्थानांतरित करना।"},"2":{"en":"Continue buying exclusively from Supplier X to protect the 15% cost savings.","hi":"15% लागत बचत बचाने के लिए केवल Supplier X से ही खरीद जारी रखना।"},"3":{"en":"Split the order with an alternative supplier to reduce risk while giving Supplier X a deadline to improve.","hi":"जोखिम घटाने के लिए ऑर्डर वैकल्पिक आपूर्तिकर्ता के साथ बाँटना तथा Supplier X को सुधार के लिए समय-सीमा देना।"},"4":{"en":"Halt all production and procurement until a third, cheaper, and flawless supplier is found.","hi":"किसी तीसरे, सस्ते और त्रुटिहीन आपूर्तिकर्ता के मिलने तक सारा उत्पादन और खरीद रोक देना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The defect rate has quadrupled and is already delaying production, so relying only on Supplier X keeps the savings but loses delivery schedules<br>Shifting everything at once removes the cost advantage, and stopping work altogether is far worse for tight margins and strict schedules<br>Splitting the order keeps part of the saving, reduces the defect risk and puts pressure on Supplier X to improve within a deadline<br>Hence splitting the order with an alternative supplier while giving Supplier X a deadline is the most appropriate action<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Split the order with an alternative supplier to reduce risk while giving Supplier X a deadline to improve..</b>","hi":"खराबी दर चार गुना हो चुकी है और उत्पादन में देरी कर रही है, अतः केवल Supplier X पर निर्भर रहना बचत बचाता है परंतु डिलीवरी कार्यक्रम गँवा देता है<br>सब कुछ एक साथ बदल देने से लागत लाभ समाप्त होता है, और काम पूरी तरह रोक देना कम मार्जिन तथा कड़े कार्यक्रम के लिए और भी हानिकारक है<br>ऑर्डर बाँटने से बचत का कुछ भाग बचता है, खराबी का जोखिम घटता है और Supplier X पर समय-सीमा में सुधार का दबाव बनता है<br>अतः ऑर्डर वैकल्पिक आपूर्तिकर्ता के साथ बाँटना तथा Supplier X को समय-सीमा देना सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त कार्यवाही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): जोखिम घटाने के लिए ऑर्डर वैकल्पिक आपूर्तिकर्ता के साथ बाँटना तथा Supplier X को सुधार के लिए समय-सीमा देना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000072105","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Which sequence is different from the others? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सा क्रम अन्य से भिन्न है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"AZBY"},"2":{"en":"CXDW"},"3":{"en":"EVFU"},"4":{"en":"GSHR"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In AZBY the pairs are A with Z and B with Y, and each letter is paired with the letter at the opposite end of the alphabet<br>CXDW pairs C with X and D with W, and EVFU pairs E with V and F with U, so the same opposite-letter rule holds ✔<br>In GSHR the pairs are G with S and H with R, but the opposite of G is T, not S, so the rule breaks ✘<br>Hence GSHR is different from the others<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): GSHR.</b>","hi":"AZBY में युग्म A के साथ Z तथा B के साथ Y हैं, और प्रत्येक अक्षर वर्णमाला के दूसरे सिरे के अक्षर के साथ जुड़ा है<br>CXDW में C के साथ X तथा D के साथ W है, और EVFU में E के साथ V तथा F के साथ U है, अतः वही विपरीत-अक्षर नियम लागू है ✔<br>GSHR में युग्म G के साथ S तथा H के साथ R हैं, परंतु G का विपरीत T है, S नहीं, अतः नियम टूट जाता है ✘<br>इसलिए GSHR अन्य से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): GSHR है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000072106","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Reports and Indices (Current)","question":{"en":"In the 2025 World Happiness Report, how many countries were included in the survey? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट 2025 में सर्वेक्षण में कितने देशों को शामिल किया गया था? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"140"},"2":{"en":"150"},"3":{"en":"146"},"4":{"en":"147"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – 147</b><br>The <b>World Happiness Report 2025</b>, released on 20 March 2025, ranked <b><u>147 countries</u></b> on the basis of life evaluations from the Gallup World Poll.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Finland</b> ranked 1<sup>st</sup> for the <b>eighth</b> consecutive year; Denmark 2<sup>nd</sup>, Iceland 3<sup>rd</sup>.<br>• <b>India</b> ranked <b>118<sup>th</sup></b>; Afghanistan was last.<br>• The report is published by the <b>Wellbeing Research Centre (Oxford)</b> with Gallup and UN SDSN.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – 147</b><br>20 मार्च 2025 को जारी <b>विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट 2025</b> ने गैलप वर्ल्ड पोल के जीवन-मूल्यांकन के आधार पर <b><u>147 देशों</u></b> को रैंक किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>फ़िनलैंड</b> लगातार <b>आठवें</b> वर्ष पहले स्थान पर; डेनमार्क दूसरे, आइसलैंड तीसरे स्थान पर।<br>• <b>भारत</b> <b>118वें</b> स्थान पर; अफ़गानिस्तान अंतिम।<br>• रिपोर्ट गैलप और UN SDSN के साथ <b>वेलबीइंग रिसर्च सेंटर (ऑक्सफोर्ड)</b> द्वारा प्रकाशित की जाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000072107","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Rocks, Continents, and Oceans","question":{"en":"Which continent is located to the west of the Indian Ocean? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"हिंद महासागर के पश्चिम में कौन-सा महाद्वीप स्थित है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Asia","hi":"एशिया"},"2":{"en":"Australia","hi":"ऑस्ट्रेलिया"},"3":{"en":"Africa","hi":"अफ्रीका"},"4":{"en":"Antarctica","hi":"अंटार्कटिका"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Africa</b><br>The Indian Ocean is bounded by <b><u>Africa</u></b> on the <b>west</b>, Asia on the north, Australia on the east and the Southern Ocean/Antarctica on the south.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Indian Ocean is the <b>third largest</b> ocean and the only ocean named after a country.<br>• Its deepest point is the <b>Java (Sunda) Trench</b>.<br>• Major islands: <b>Madagascar</b> (largest), Sri Lanka, Maldives, Mauritius.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अफ्रीका</b><br>हिंद महासागर के <b>पश्चिम</b> में <b><u>अफ्रीका</u></b>, उत्तर में एशिया, पूर्व में ऑस्ट्रेलिया और दक्षिण में दक्षिणी महासागर/अंटार्कटिका है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• हिंद महासागर <b>तीसरा सबसे बड़ा</b> महासागर है और किसी देश के नाम पर रखा गया एकमात्र महासागर है।<br>• इसका सबसे गहरा बिंदु <b>जावा (सुंडा) गर्त</b> है।<br>• प्रमुख द्वीप: <b>मेडागास्कर</b> (सबसे बड़ा), श्रीलंका, मालदीव, मॉरीशस।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000072108","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"The \"National Digital Health Mission (NDHM)\" aims to create an integrated digital health infrastructure for India. Which of the following is a core feature envisioned under this mission? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\"राष्ट्रीय डिजिटल स्वास्थ्य मिशन (NDHM)\" का उद्देश्य भारत के लिए एकीकृत डिजिटल स्वास्थ्य अवसंरचना बनाना है। इस मिशन के तहत परिकल्पित एक मुख्य विशेषता निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Providing free generic medicines to all citizens through online platforms.","hi":"ऑनलाइन प्लेटफ़ॉर्म के माध्यम से सभी नागरिकों को मुफ्त जेनेरिक दवाएँ उपलब्ध कराना।"},"2":{"en":"Creating a unique health ID for every citizen to maintain their health records digitally.","hi":"प्रत्येक नागरिक के स्वास्थ्य रिकॉर्ड डिजिटल रूप से रखने के लिए एक विशिष्ट स्वास्थ्य ID बनाना।"},"3":{"en":"Establishing a network of telemedicine centers in all villages.","hi":"सभी गाँवों में टेलीमेडिसिन केंद्रों का नेटवर्क स्थापित करना।"},"4":{"en":"Mandating the use of electronic health records by all private hospitals.","hi":"सभी निजी अस्पतालों के लिए इलेक्ट्रॉनिक स्वास्थ्य रिकॉर्ड का उपयोग अनिवार्य करना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Creating a unique health ID for every citizen to maintain their health records digitally.</b><br>The core feature of NDHM is a <b><u>unique Health ID</u></b> (now the <b>ABHA – Ayushman Bharat Health Account</b>) for every citizen, through which health records can be stored and shared digitally with consent.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• NDHM was announced on <b>15 August 2020</b> and renamed <b>Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM)</b> in <b>September 2021</b>.<br>• Implemented by the <b>National Health Authority (NHA)</b>.<br>• ABHA number is a <b>14-digit</b> health ID.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – प्रत्येक नागरिक के स्वास्थ्य रिकॉर्ड डिजिटल रूप से रखने के लिए एक विशिष्ट स्वास्थ्य ID बनाना।</b><br>NDHM की मुख्य विशेषता प्रत्येक नागरिक के लिए एक <b><u>विशिष्ट स्वास्थ्य ID</u></b> (अब <b>ABHA – आयुष्मान भारत हेल्थ अकाउंट</b>) है, जिसके माध्यम से सहमति से स्वास्थ्य रिकॉर्ड डिजिटल रूप में रखे और साझा किए जा सकते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NDHM की घोषणा <b>15 अगस्त 2020</b> को हुई और <b>सितंबर 2021</b> में इसका नाम <b>आयुष्मान भारत डिजिटल मिशन (ABDM)</b> रखा गया।<br>• <b>राष्ट्रीय स्वास्थ्य प्राधिकरण (NHA)</b> द्वारा कार्यान्वित।<br>• ABHA संख्या <b>14 अंकों</b> की स्वास्थ्य ID है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000072109","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"The \"National Policy on Education (NPE)\" has been revised several times since independence. The latest iteration is the NEP 2020. Which of the following principles is a significant guiding principle of the NEP 2020? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\"राष्ट्रीय शिक्षा नीति (NPE)\" स्वतंत्रता के बाद कई बार संशोधित की गई है। नवीनतम संस्करण NEP 2020 है। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा सिद्धांत NEP 2020 का एक महत्वपूर्ण मार्गदर्शक सिद्धांत है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Strict standardization of curriculum and assessment across all states.","hi":"सभी राज्यों में पाठ्यक्रम और मूल्यांकन का कठोर मानकीकरण।"},"2":{"en":"Emphasis on rote learning and memorization of facts.","hi":"रटकर सीखने और तथ्यों को याद करने पर ज़ोर।"},"3":{"en":"Promoting critical thinking, creativity, and conceptual understanding.","hi":"आलोचनात्मक चिंतन, रचनात्मकता और वैचारिक समझ को बढ़ावा देना।"},"4":{"en":"Early specialization in specific academic disciplines from the secondary level.","hi":"माध्यमिक स्तर से विशिष्ट शैक्षणिक विषयों में प्रारंभिक विशेषज्ञता।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Promoting critical thinking, creativity, and conceptual understanding.</b><br>NEP 2020 moves away from rote learning and emphasises <b><u>critical thinking, creativity and conceptual understanding</u></b>, with flexibility in subject choice and no hard separation between streams.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• NEP 2020 was drafted by a committee headed by <b>Dr. K. Kasturirangan</b>.<br>• It replaces the 10+2 structure with <b>5+3+3+4</b>.<br>• Earlier policies: <b>NPE 1968</b> (Kothari Commission) and <b>NPE 1986</b> (revised in 1992).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – आलोचनात्मक चिंतन, रचनात्मकता और वैचारिक समझ को बढ़ावा देना।</b><br>NEP 2020 रटकर सीखने से हटकर <b><u>आलोचनात्मक चिंतन, रचनात्मकता और वैचारिक समझ</u></b> पर ज़ोर देती है, जिसमें विषय चयन में लचीलापन है और धाराओं के बीच कठोर विभाजन नहीं है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NEP 2020 का प्रारूप <b>डॉ. के. कस्तूरीरंगन</b> की अध्यक्षता वाली समिति ने तैयार किया।<br>• इसने 10+2 संरचना के स्थान पर <b>5+3+3+4</b> संरचना अपनाई।<br>• पूर्व नीतियाँ: <b>NPE 1968</b> (कोठारी आयोग) और <b>NPE 1986</b> (1992 में संशोधित)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000072110","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which Indian athlete is known for her achievements in sprint running and is often referred to as \"Dhing Express\"? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सी भारतीय एथलीट स्प्रिंट दौड़ में अपनी उपलब्धियों के लिए जानी जाती है और जिसे अक्सर \"ढिंग एक्सप्रेस\" कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"P.T. Usha","hi":"पी.टी. उषा"},"2":{"en":"Anju Bobby George","hi":"अंजू बॉबी जॉर्ज"},"3":{"en":"Hima Das","hi":"हिमा दास"},"4":{"en":"Dutee Chand","hi":"दुती चंद"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Hima Das</b><br><b><u>Hima Das</u></b>, from <b>Dhing village in Nagaon district, Assam</b>, is called the \"Dhing Express\". In 2018 she became the first Indian to win a gold at the <b>IAAF World U-20 Championships</b> (400 m).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>P.T. Usha</b> – \"Payyoli Express\"; current President of the <b>Indian Olympic Association</b>.<br>• <b>Anju Bobby George</b> – first Indian to win a medal at the World Athletics Championships (long jump bronze, 2003).<br>• <b>Dutee Chand</b> – national record holder in women's 100 m.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – हिमा दास</b><br><b>असम के नगाँव ज़िले के ढिंग गाँव</b> की <b><u>हिमा दास</u></b> को \"ढिंग एक्सप्रेस\" कहा जाता है। 2018 में वह <b>IAAF विश्व अंडर-20 चैंपियनशिप</b> (400 मीटर) में स्वर्ण जीतने वाली पहली भारतीय बनीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>पी.टी. उषा</b> – \"पय्योली एक्सप्रेस\"; वर्तमान में <b>भारतीय ओलंपिक संघ</b> की अध्यक्ष।<br>• <b>अंजू बॉबी जॉर्ज</b> – विश्व एथलेटिक्स चैंपियनशिप में पदक जीतने वाली पहली भारतीय (लंबी कूद कांस्य, 2003)।<br>• <b>दुती चंद</b> – महिला 100 मीटर की राष्ट्रीय रिकॉर्डधारी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000072111","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"The Singh Sisters from Punjab contributed to India's rise in which underrepresented court sport? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पंजाब की सिंह बहनों ने किस कम प्रतिनिधित्व वाले कोर्ट खेल में भारत के उत्थान में योगदान दिया? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tennis","hi":"टेनिस"},"2":{"en":"Handball","hi":"हैंडबॉल"},"3":{"en":"Basketball","hi":"बास्केटबॉल"},"4":{"en":"Kho-Kho","hi":"खो-खो"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Basketball</b><br>The <b>Singh Sisters</b> – <b>Prashanti, Akanksha, Divya, Pratima</b> and Priyanka Singh – represented India in <b><u>basketball</u></b> and played a major role in the growth of women's basketball in the country.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Prashanti Singh</b> received the <b>Arjuna Award (2017)</b> and the <b>Padma Shri (2019)</b>.<br>• Basketball was invented by <b>James Naismith</b> in <b>1891</b>; 5 players per side.<br>• Governing body: <b>Basketball Federation of India</b>; international body <b>FIBA</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – बास्केटबॉल</b><br><b>सिंह बहनों</b> – <b>प्रशांति, आकांक्षा, दिव्या, प्रतिमा</b> और प्रियंका सिंह – ने <b><u>बास्केटबॉल</u></b> में भारत का प्रतिनिधित्व किया और देश में महिला बास्केटबॉल के विकास में बड़ी भूमिका निभाई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>प्रशांति सिंह</b> को <b>अर्जुन पुरस्कार (2017)</b> और <b>पद्म श्री (2019)</b> मिला।<br>• बास्केटबॉल का आविष्कार <b>जेम्स नाइस्मिथ</b> ने <b>1891</b> में किया; प्रत्येक टीम में 5 खिलाड़ी।<br>• शासी निकाय: <b>बास्केटबॉल फेडरेशन ऑफ इंडिया</b>; अंतर्राष्ट्रीय निकाय <b>FIBA</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000072112","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Where was the location of the 2017 Senior National Judo Championships? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"2017 सीनियर राष्ट्रीय जूडो चैंपियनशिप का आयोजन स्थल कहाँ था? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Jaipur","hi":"जयपुर"},"2":{"en":"Lucknow","hi":"लखनऊ"},"3":{"en":"Guwahati","hi":"गुवाहाटी"},"4":{"en":"Chennai","hi":"चेन्नई"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Chennai</b><br>The <b>Senior National Judo Championships 2016-17</b> were held in <b><u>Chennai</u></b> (Tamil Nadu) on <b>26–27 February 2017</b>, organised under the Judo Federation of India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Judo originated in <b>Japan</b>; founded by <b>Jigoro Kano</b> in 1882.<br>• Judo became an Olympic sport at <b>Tokyo 1964</b>.<br>• Judo terms: <b>Ippon, Waza-ari, Tatami, Judogi</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – चेन्नई</b><br><b>सीनियर राष्ट्रीय जूडो चैंपियनशिप 2016-17</b> का आयोजन <b>26–27 फरवरी 2017</b> को <b><u>चेन्नई</u></b> (तमिलनाडु) में जूडो फेडरेशन ऑफ इंडिया के अधीन किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• जूडो की उत्पत्ति <b>जापान</b> में हुई; 1882 में <b>जिगोरो कानो</b> ने इसकी स्थापना की।<br>• जूडो <b>टोक्यो 1964</b> में ओलंपिक खेल बना।<br>• जूडो की शब्दावली: <b>इप्पोन, वाज़ा-अरी, तातामी, जूडोगी</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000072113","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"According to the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam (BSA), which of the following principles regarding conclusive proof is TRUE? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम (BSA) के अनुसार निश्चायक सबूत के संबंध में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा सिद्धांत सही है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It requires two eyewitnesses","hi":"इसके लिए दो चश्मदीद गवाह आवश्यक हैं"},"2":{"en":"It applies only in civil cases","hi":"यह केवल दीवानी मामलों में लागू होता है"},"3":{"en":"It is final and cannot be disputed in court","hi":"यह अंतिम है और न्यायालय में इसे विवादित नहीं किया जा सकता"},"4":{"en":"It can be rebutted by expert testimony","hi":"विशेषज्ञ साक्ष्य द्वारा इसका खंडन किया जा सकता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – It is final and cannot be disputed in court</b><br>Under the BSA (Section 2), when a fact is declared to be <b>conclusive proof</b> of another, the Court must regard the other as proved and <b><u>shall not allow evidence to disprove it</u></b>. It is final.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>\"May presume\"</b> – Court may regard a fact as proved or ask for proof (rebuttable).<br>• <b>\"Shall presume\"</b> – Court must regard the fact as proved unless disproved.<br>• BSA replaced the <b>Indian Evidence Act, 1872</b> from <b>1 July 2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – यह अंतिम है और न्यायालय में इसे विवादित नहीं किया जा सकता</b><br>BSA (धारा 2) के अनुसार, जब किसी तथ्य को दूसरे तथ्य का <b>निश्चायक सबूत (Conclusive proof)</b> घोषित किया जाता है, तो न्यायालय दूसरे तथ्य को सिद्ध मानेगा और <b><u>उसे गलत साबित करने के लिए साक्ष्य की अनुमति नहीं देगा</u></b>। यह अंतिम है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>\"उपधारणा कर सकेगा (May presume)\"</b> – न्यायालय तथ्य को सिद्ध मान सकता है या सबूत माँग सकता है (खंडनीय)।<br>• <b>\"उपधारणा करेगा (Shall presume)\"</b> – न्यायालय तथ्य को तब तक सिद्ध मानेगा जब तक उसका खंडन न हो।<br>• BSA ने <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से <b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 1872</b> का स्थान लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000072114","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who is the ninth chairperson of the National Commission for Women (NCW)? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"राष्ट्रीय महिला आयोग (NCW) की नौवीं अध्यक्ष कौन हैं? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rekha Sharma","hi":"रेखा शर्मा"},"2":{"en":"Lalitha Kumaramangalam","hi":"ललिता कुमारमंगलम"},"3":{"en":"Vijaya Rahatkar","hi":"विजया रहाटकर"},"4":{"en":"Smriti Irani","hi":"स्मृति ईरानी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Vijaya Rahatkar</b><br><b><u>Vijaya Rahatkar</u></b> was appointed the <b>9<sup>th</sup> Chairperson of NCW</b> in <b>October 2024</b> for a three-year term, succeeding Rekha Sharma.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• NCW is a <b>statutory body</b> set up in <b>January 1992</b> under the <b>NCW Act, 1990</b>.<br>• First chairperson: <b>Jayanti Patnaik</b>.<br>• Rekha Sharma was the 8<sup>th</sup> chairperson; <b>Lalitha Kumaramangalam</b> was the 7<sup>th</sup>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – विजया रहाटकर</b><br><b><u>विजया रहाटकर</u></b> को <b>अक्टूबर 2024</b> में तीन वर्ष के कार्यकाल के लिए रेखा शर्मा के बाद <b>NCW की 9वीं अध्यक्ष</b> नियुक्त किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NCW <b>राष्ट्रीय महिला आयोग अधिनियम, 1990</b> के तहत <b>जनवरी 1992</b> में गठित एक <b>सांविधिक निकाय (Statutory body)</b> है।<br>• पहली अध्यक्ष: <b>जयंती पटनायक</b>।<br>• रेखा शर्मा 8वीं और <b>ललिता कुमारमंगलम</b> 7वीं अध्यक्ष थीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000072115","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: State Legislature","question":{"en":"Which one of the following Chief Ministers of West Bengal was sworn in May 2011? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पश्चिम बंगाल के निम्नलिखित मुख्यमंत्रियों में से किसने मई 2011 में शपथ ली? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mamata Banerjee","hi":"ममता बनर्जी"},"2":{"en":"Suvendu Adhikari","hi":"शुभेंदु अधिकारी"},"3":{"en":"Partha Chatterjee","hi":"पार्थ चटर्जी"},"4":{"en":"Abhishek Banerjee","hi":"अभिषेक बनर्जी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Mamata Banerjee</b><br><b><u>Mamata Banerjee</u></b> was sworn in as Chief Minister of West Bengal on <b>20 May 2011</b>, ending 34 years of Left Front rule; she became the state's <b>first woman Chief Minister</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Mamata Banerjee founded the <b>All India Trinamool Congress</b> in <b>1998</b>.<br>• Her predecessor was <b>Buddhadeb Bhattacharjee</b> (CPI-M).<br>• <b>Jyoti Basu</b> was the longest-serving CM of West Bengal (1977–2000).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – ममता बनर्जी</b><br><b><u>ममता बनर्जी</u></b> ने <b>20 मई 2011</b> को पश्चिम बंगाल की मुख्यमंत्री के रूप में शपथ ली, जिससे 34 वर्षों का वाम मोर्चा शासन समाप्त हुआ; वह राज्य की <b>पहली महिला मुख्यमंत्री</b> बनीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ममता बनर्जी ने <b>1998</b> में <b>अखिल भारतीय तृणमूल कांग्रेस</b> की स्थापना की।<br>• उनके पूर्ववर्ती <b>बुद्धदेव भट्टाचार्य</b> (CPI-M) थे।<br>• <b>ज्योति बसु</b> पश्चिम बंगाल के सबसे लंबे समय तक रहे मुख्यमंत्री थे (1977–2000)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000072116","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Vedic Age","question":{"en":"Which of the following is NOT one of the Rig Vedic Gods? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन ऋग्वैदिक देवताओं में से एक नहीं है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Indra","hi":"इंद्र"},"2":{"en":"Pasupathi","hi":"पशुपति"},"3":{"en":"Prithvi","hi":"पृथ्वी"},"4":{"en":"Varuna","hi":"वरुण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Pasupathi</b><br><b>Indra, Prithvi and Varuna</b> are Rig Vedic deities. <b><u>Pashupati</u></b> (Shiva as lord of animals) became prominent in <b>later times</b>; in the Rig Veda, Rudra is only a minor god.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Indra</b> (Purandara) is the most important Rig Vedic god, with <b>250 hymns</b>; <b>Agni</b> is second with 200 hymns.<br>• <b>Varuna</b> – god of water and upholder of cosmic order (<b>Rita</b>).<br>• A \"proto-Shiva/Pashupati\" seal was found at <b>Mohenjo-daro</b> (Indus Valley).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पशुपति</b><br><b>इंद्र, पृथ्वी और वरुण</b> ऋग्वैदिक देवता हैं। <b><u>पशुपति</u></b> (पशुओं के स्वामी के रूप में शिव) <b>बाद के काल</b> में प्रमुख हुए; ऋग्वेद में रुद्र एक गौण देवता हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>इंद्र</b> (पुरंदर) सबसे महत्वपूर्ण ऋग्वैदिक देवता हैं, जिनके <b>250 सूक्त</b> हैं; <b>अग्नि</b> 200 सूक्तों के साथ दूसरे स्थान पर हैं।<br>• <b>वरुण</b> – जल के देवता और ब्रह्मांडीय व्यवस्था (<b>ऋत</b>) के रक्षक।<br>• <b>मोहनजोदड़ो</b> (सिंधु घाटी) से \"आद्य-शिव/पशुपति\" मुहर मिली है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000072117","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"The highest amount of sugarcane is produced in: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"गन्ने का सर्वाधिक उत्पादन कहाँ होता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Uttar Pradesh","hi":"उत्तर प्रदेश"},"2":{"en":"Andhra Pradesh","hi":"आंध्र प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Haryana","hi":"हरियाणा"},"4":{"en":"Punjab","hi":"पंजाब"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Uttar Pradesh</b><br><b><u>Uttar Pradesh</u></b> is the largest producer of sugarcane in India, contributing nearly <b>half</b> of the country's output, followed by <b>Maharashtra and Karnataka</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India is the <b>second largest</b> producer of sugarcane in the world after <b>Brazil</b>.<br>• Sugarcane is a <b>Kharif</b> crop needing 21–27°C temperature and 75–100 cm rainfall.<br>• <b>Indian Institute of Sugarcane Research</b> is in <b>Lucknow</b>; Sugarcane Breeding Institute is in <b>Coimbatore</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – उत्तर प्रदेश</b><br><b><u>उत्तर प्रदेश</u></b> भारत में गन्ने का सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक है, जो देश के उत्पादन का लगभग <b>आधा</b> देता है; इसके बाद <b>महाराष्ट्र और कर्नाटक</b> हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत <b>ब्राज़ील</b> के बाद विश्व में गन्ने का <b>दूसरा सबसे बड़ा</b> उत्पादक है।<br>• गन्ना <b>खरीफ</b> फसल है, जिसे 21–27°C तापमान और 75–100 cm वर्षा चाहिए।<br>• <b>भारतीय गन्ना अनुसंधान संस्थान</b> <b>लखनऊ</b> में और गन्ना प्रजनन संस्थान <b>कोयंबटूर</b> में है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000072118","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Making of Constitution","question":{"en":"What major administrative change was introduced by the Charter Act of 1853? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1853 के चार्टर अधिनियम द्वारा कौन-सा प्रमुख प्रशासनिक परिवर्तन किया गया? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Created provincial assemblies with elected Indian members","hi":"निर्वाचित भारतीय सदस्यों के साथ प्रांतीय सभाएँ बनाईं"},"2":{"en":"Introduced bicameral legislature in British India","hi":"ब्रिटिश भारत में द्विसदनीय विधायिका शुरू की"},"3":{"en":"Separated legislative and executive functions of the Council","hi":"परिषद के विधायी और कार्यकारी कार्यों को पृथक किया"},"4":{"en":"Gave voting rights to landed Indians","hi":"भूमिधारी भारतीयों को मताधिकार दिया"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Separated legislative and executive functions of the Council</b><br>The <b>Charter Act of 1853</b> <b><u>separated the legislative and executive functions</u></b> of the Governor-General's Council by adding six legislative members, forming a separate <b>Central Legislative Council</b> (Indian mini-Parliament).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It introduced <b>open competition</b> for the Indian Civil Service (Macaulay Committee, 1854).<br>• It was the <b>last</b> of the Charter Acts.<br>• It introduced <b>local representation</b> in the legislative council for the first time.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – परिषद के विधायी और कार्यकारी कार्यों को पृथक किया</b><br><b>1853 के चार्टर अधिनियम</b> ने छह विधायी सदस्य जोड़कर गवर्नर-जनरल की परिषद के <b><u>विधायी और कार्यकारी कार्यों को पृथक</u></b> किया और एक अलग <b>केंद्रीय विधान परिषद</b> (भारतीय लघु संसद) बनाई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसने भारतीय सिविल सेवा के लिए <b>खुली प्रतियोगिता</b> शुरू की (मैकाले समिति, 1854)।<br>• यह चार्टर अधिनियमों में <b>अंतिम</b> था।<br>• इसने पहली बार विधान परिषद में <b>स्थानीय प्रतिनिधित्व</b> शुरू किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000072119","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: State News","question":{"en":"The state of Uttarakhand has recently taken steps towards implementing a Uniform Civil Code. What is a key feature of the proposed Uniform Civil Code(UCC) in Uttarakhand? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उत्तराखंड राज्य ने हाल ही में समान नागरिक संहिता लागू करने की दिशा में कदम उठाए हैं। उत्तराखंड में प्रस्तावित समान नागरिक संहिता (UCC) की एक प्रमुख विशेषता क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mandatory religious conversions.","hi":"अनिवार्य धर्मांतरण।"},"2":{"en":"Uniform laws for marriage, divorce, and inheritance, excluding tribal communities.","hi":"जनजातीय समुदायों को छोड़कर विवाह, तलाक और उत्तराधिकार के लिए एकसमान कानून।"},"3":{"en":"Abolition of all existing personal laws immediately.","hi":"सभी मौजूदा व्यक्तिगत कानूनों का तत्काल उन्मूलन।"},"4":{"en":"Introduction of Sharia law for all citizens.","hi":"सभी नागरिकों के लिए शरिया कानून लागू करना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Uniform laws for marriage, divorce, and inheritance, excluding tribal communities.</b><br>Uttarakhand's UCC provides <b><u>common laws on marriage, divorce, inheritance and live-in relationships</u></b> for all residents, but <b>Scheduled Tribes are excluded</b> from its scope.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Uttarakhand became the <b>first state after Independence</b> to implement a UCC, from <b>27 January 2025</b>.<br>• The draft was prepared by a committee headed by <b>Justice (Retd.) Ranjana Prakash Desai</b>.<br>• UCC is a Directive Principle under <b>Article 44</b>; <b>Goa</b> already follows the Portuguese Civil Code of 1867.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – जनजातीय समुदायों को छोड़कर विवाह, तलाक और उत्तराधिकार के लिए एकसमान कानून।</b><br>उत्तराखंड की UCC सभी निवासियों के लिए <b><u>विवाह, तलाक, उत्तराधिकार और लिव-इन संबंधों पर समान कानून</u></b> देती है, परंतु <b>अनुसूचित जनजातियों को इसके दायरे से बाहर</b> रखा गया है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उत्तराखंड <b>27 जनवरी 2025</b> से UCC लागू करने वाला <b>स्वतंत्रता के बाद पहला राज्य</b> बना।<br>• इसका मसौदा <b>न्यायमूर्ति (सेवानिवृत्त) रंजना प्रकाश देसाई</b> की अध्यक्षता वाली समिति ने तैयार किया।<br>• UCC <b>अनुच्छेद 44</b> के तहत नीति निदेशक तत्व है; <b>गोवा</b> में पहले से 1867 की पुर्तगाली नागरिक संहिता लागू है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000072120","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: South Indian History & Tripartite Struggle and Cholas","question":{"en":"In the epic “Silappadikaram”, which capital city was ultimately destroyed by fire due to Kannagi’s curse? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"महाकाव्य “शिलप्पादिकारम” में कन्नगी के श्राप के कारण कौन-सी राजधानी अंततः आग से नष्ट हो गई? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Madurai city","hi":"मदुरै नगर"},"2":{"en":"Uraiyur city","hi":"उरैयूर नगर"},"3":{"en":"Puhar city","hi":"पुहार नगर"},"4":{"en":"Vanji city","hi":"वंजी नगर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Madurai city</b><br>In <b>Silappadikaram</b>, Kovalan is wrongly executed by the <b>Pandya king</b>. His wife <b>Kannagi</b> proves his innocence and, in anger, curses <b><u>Madurai</u></b>, the Pandya capital, which is consumed by fire.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Silappadikaram was written by <b>Ilango Adigal</b>; it is one of the <b>Five Great Epics</b> of Tamil literature.<br>• Its sequel <b>Manimekalai</b> was written by <b>Sittalai Sattanar</b>.<br>• <b>Puhar</b> was the Chola port; <b>Uraiyur</b> the Chola capital; <b>Vanji</b> the Chera capital.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मदुरै नगर</b><br><b>शिलप्पादिकारम</b> में <b>पांड्य राजा</b> द्वारा कोवलन को गलत तरीके से मृत्युदंड दिया जाता है। उसकी पत्नी <b>कन्नगी</b> उसकी निर्दोषता सिद्ध करती है और क्रोध में पांड्य राजधानी <b><u>मदुरै</u></b> को श्राप देती है, जो आग में जल जाती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• शिलप्पादिकारम <b>इलंगो आडिगल</b> ने लिखा; यह तमिल साहित्य के <b>पाँच महाकाव्यों</b> में से एक है।<br>• इसका अगला भाग <b>मणिमेकलै</b> <b>सीतलै सत्तनार</b> ने लिखा।<br>• <b>पुहार</b> चोल बंदरगाह; <b>उरैयूर</b> चोल राजधानी; <b>वंजी</b> चेर राजधानी थी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000072121","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"The Vice-President is the second-highest constitutional authority of India under which Part of the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उपराष्ट्रपति भारतीय संविधान के किस भाग के अंतर्गत भारत का दूसरा सर्वोच्च संवैधानिक प्राधिकारी है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Part IV","hi":"भाग IV"},"2":{"en":"Part V","hi":"भाग V"},"3":{"en":"Part VI","hi":"भाग VI"},"4":{"en":"Part III","hi":"भाग III"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Part V</b><br>The Vice-President is provided under <b>Articles 63–71</b> in <b><u>Part V</u></b> (The Union) of the Constitution.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Vice-President is the <b>ex-officio Chairman of the Rajya Sabha</b> (Article 64).<br>• Elected by an electoral college of <b>members of both Houses of Parliament</b>.<br>• <b>Part III</b> – Fundamental Rights; <b>Part IV</b> – DPSP; <b>Part VI</b> – The States.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भाग V</b><br>उपराष्ट्रपति का प्रावधान संविधान के <b><u>भाग V</u></b> (संघ) में <b>अनुच्छेद 63–71</b> के अंतर्गत है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उपराष्ट्रपति <b>राज्यसभा के पदेन सभापति</b> होते हैं (अनुच्छेद 64)।<br>• <b>संसद के दोनों सदनों के सदस्यों</b> वाले निर्वाचक मंडल द्वारा निर्वाचित।<br>• <b>भाग III</b> – मौलिक अधिकार; <b>भाग IV</b> – नीति निदेशक तत्व; <b>भाग VI</b> – राज्य।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000072122","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Electricity","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the SI unit of resistivity? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा प्रतिरोधकता का SI मात्रक है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ohm-meter","hi":"ओम-मीटर"},"2":{"en":"Ohm","hi":"ओम"},"3":{"en":"Coulomb","hi":"कूलॉम"},"4":{"en":"Ampere-meter","hi":"एम्पियर-मीटर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Ohm-meter</b><br>From \\(R = \\rho\\frac{l}{A}\\), \\(\\rho = \\frac{RA}{l}\\), so the unit of resistivity is \\(\\frac{\\Omega \\cdot m^2}{m}\\) = <b><u>ohm-metre (Ω·m)</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Resistivity depends on the <b>nature of material and temperature</b>, not on its length or area.<br>• <b>Ohm</b> – unit of resistance; <b>Coulomb</b> – unit of charge.<br>• Conductivity is the reciprocal of resistivity; its SI unit is <b>siemens per metre (S/m)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – ओम-मीटर</b><br>\\(R = \\rho\\frac{l}{A}\\) से \\(\\rho = \\frac{RA}{l}\\), अतः प्रतिरोधकता (Resistivity) का मात्रक \\(\\frac{\\Omega \\cdot m^2}{m}\\) = <b><u>ओम-मीटर (Ω·m)</u></b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रतिरोधकता <b>पदार्थ की प्रकृति और ताप</b> पर निर्भर करती है, लंबाई या क्षेत्रफल पर नहीं।<br>• <b>ओम</b> – प्रतिरोध का मात्रक; <b>कूलॉम</b> – आवेश का मात्रक।<br>• चालकता (Conductivity) प्रतिरोधकता का व्युत्क्रम है; इसका SI मात्रक <b>सीमेंस प्रति मीटर (S/m)</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000072123","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Centre-State Relations","question":{"en":"In India, a law made by Parliament under Article 249 on a subject in the State List remains in force: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में, अनुच्छेद 249 के तहत राज्य सूची के किसी विषय पर संसद द्वारा बनाया गया कानून लागू रहता है: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Permanently unless repealed by Parliament","hi":"स्थायी रूप से, जब तक संसद उसे निरसित न करे"},"2":{"en":"Only during the validity of the Rajya Sabha resolution","hi":"केवल राज्यसभा संकल्प की वैधता के दौरान"},"3":{"en":"For six months after the resolution ceases to be in force","hi":"संकल्प के प्रवृत्त न रहने के छह माह बाद तक"},"4":{"en":"Till the concerned state legislature repeals it","hi":"जब तक संबंधित राज्य विधानमंडल उसे निरसित न करे"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – For six months after the resolution ceases to be in force</b><br>Under <b>Article 249</b>, a law made on a State subject in the national interest (after a Rajya Sabha resolution) <b><u>ceases to have effect six months after the resolution ceases to be in force</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Rajya Sabha resolution needs a <b>two-thirds majority of members present and voting</b>.<br>• The resolution is valid for <b>one year</b> and can be renewed any number of times, one year at a time.<br>• <b>Article 250</b> – Parliament can legislate on State subjects during a National Emergency.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – संकल्प के प्रवृत्त न रहने के छह माह बाद तक</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 249</b> के तहत (राज्यसभा संकल्प के बाद) राष्ट्रीय हित में राज्य विषय पर बना कानून <b><u>संकल्प के प्रवृत्त न रहने के छह माह बाद प्रभावहीन</u></b> हो जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• राज्यसभा संकल्प के लिए <b>उपस्थित और मतदान करने वाले सदस्यों का दो-तिहाई बहुमत</b> आवश्यक है।<br>• संकल्प <b>एक वर्ष</b> के लिए वैध है और एक-एक वर्ष के लिए कितनी भी बार बढ़ाया जा सकता है।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 250</b> – राष्ट्रीय आपातकाल में संसद राज्य विषयों पर कानून बना सकती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000072124","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"The growth of Business Process Outsourcing (BPO) in India is mainly associated with which 1991 economic reform? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में बिज़नेस प्रोसेस आउटसोर्सिंग (BPO) की वृद्धि मुख्य रूप से 1991 के किस आर्थिक सुधार से जुड़ी है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Globalisation reform","hi":"वैश्वीकरण सुधार"},"2":{"en":"Privatisation reform","hi":"निजीकरण सुधार"},"3":{"en":"Liberalisation reform","hi":"उदारीकरण सुधार"},"4":{"en":"Disinvestment reform","hi":"विनिवेश सुधार"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Globalisation reform</b><br><b>Outsourcing</b> is a key outcome of <b><u>globalisation</u></b>: integration with the world economy and better IT links allowed foreign firms to shift BPO, call-centre and back-office work to India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• NCERT lists <b>outsourcing</b> and <b>WTO membership</b> as major outcomes of globalisation.<br>• India is a founding member of the <b>WTO (1995)</b>.<br>• India's low-cost skilled, English-speaking workforce made it a <b>global BPO hub</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – वैश्वीकरण सुधार</b><br><b>आउटसोर्सिंग</b> <b><u>वैश्वीकरण (Globalisation)</u></b> का प्रमुख परिणाम है: विश्व अर्थव्यवस्था से जुड़ाव और बेहतर IT संपर्क से विदेशी कंपनियों ने BPO, कॉल-सेंटर और बैक-ऑफिस का कार्य भारत को सौंपा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NCERT <b>आउटसोर्सिंग</b> और <b>WTO सदस्यता</b> को वैश्वीकरण के प्रमुख परिणाम बताता है।<br>• भारत <b>WTO (1995)</b> का संस्थापक सदस्य है।<br>• भारत के कम लागत वाले कुशल, अंग्रेज़ी-भाषी कार्यबल ने इसे <b>वैश्विक BPO केंद्र</b> बनाया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000072125","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"In the Human Development Index (HDI), the dimension of a decent standard of living is primarily measured by which of the following? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मानव विकास सूचकांक (HDI) में उचित जीवन स्तर के आयाम को मुख्य रूप से किसके द्वारा मापा जाता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Access to Transportation (AT) per capita","hi":"प्रति व्यक्ति परिवहन तक पहुँच (AT)"},"2":{"en":"Population Density (PD) per square kilometer","hi":"प्रति वर्ग किलोमीटर जनसंख्या घनत्व (PD)"},"3":{"en":"Availability of Housing (AH) per household","hi":"प्रति परिवार आवास की उपलब्धता (AH)"},"4":{"en":"Gross National Income (GNI) per capita","hi":"प्रति व्यक्ति सकल राष्ट्रीय आय (GNI)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Gross National Income (GNI) per capita</b><br>In the HDI, a <b>decent standard of living</b> is measured by <b><u>GNI per capita</u></b> (in PPP US dollars, on a log scale).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Long and healthy life</b> – life expectancy at birth.<br>• <b>Knowledge</b> – mean years of schooling and expected years of schooling.<br>• Before 2010, the income indicator was <b>GDP per capita</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – प्रति व्यक्ति सकल राष्ट्रीय आय (GNI)</b><br>HDI में <b>उचित जीवन स्तर</b> को <b><u>प्रति व्यक्ति GNI</u></b> (PPP अमेरिकी डॉलर में, लघुगणकीय पैमाने पर) से मापा जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>दीर्घ और स्वस्थ जीवन</b> – जन्म के समय जीवन प्रत्याशा।<br>• <b>ज्ञान</b> – स्कूली शिक्षा के औसत वर्ष और अपेक्षित वर्ष।<br>• 2010 से पहले आय संकेतक <b>प्रति व्यक्ति GDP</b> था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000072126","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which of the following sectors was intended to increase its international competitiveness through the trade and investment policy reforms introduced under the Economic Reforms of 1991? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 के आर्थिक सुधारों के तहत लागू व्यापार और निवेश नीति सुधारों के माध्यम से किस क्षेत्र की अंतर्राष्ट्रीय प्रतिस्पर्धात्मकता बढ़ाने का लक्ष्य था? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Agricultural production and rural employment","hi":"कृषि उत्पादन और ग्रामीण रोज़गार"},"2":{"en":"Industrial production and foreign technology","hi":"औद्योगिक उत्पादन और विदेशी प्रौद्योगिकी"},"3":{"en":"Public sector production and domestic investment","hi":"सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र उत्पादन और घरेलू निवेश"},"4":{"en":"Agricultural exports and public investment","hi":"कृषि निर्यात और सार्वजनिक निवेश"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Industrial production and foreign technology</b><br>As per NCERT, trade and investment policy reforms aimed to <b>increase the international competitiveness of <u>industrial production</u></b> and attract <b><u>foreign investment and technology</u></b> into the economy.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Reforms included <b>removal of quantitative restrictions</b> on imports and exports and <b>reduction of tariff rates</b>.<br>• Industrial licensing was abolished except for a few industries (now only <b>3</b>).<br>• The <b>exchange rate</b> was made market-determined after devaluation in 1991.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – औद्योगिक उत्पादन और विदेशी प्रौद्योगिकी</b><br>NCERT के अनुसार व्यापार और निवेश नीति सुधारों का उद्देश्य <b><u>औद्योगिक उत्पादन</u> की अंतर्राष्ट्रीय प्रतिस्पर्धात्मकता बढ़ाना</b> और अर्थव्यवस्था में <b><u>विदेशी निवेश और प्रौद्योगिकी</u></b> आकर्षित करना था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सुधारों में आयात-निर्यात पर <b>मात्रात्मक प्रतिबंधों को हटाना</b> और <b>सीमा शुल्क दरों में कमी</b> शामिल थी।<br>• कुछ उद्योगों को छोड़कर औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग समाप्त की गई (अब केवल <b>3</b>)।<br>• 1991 में अवमूल्यन के बाद <b>विनिमय दर</b> बाज़ार-निर्धारित की गई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000072127","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Electricity","question":{"en":"The capacitance of a capacitor is doubled, while the potential difference across it is reduced to half its initial value. By what factor does the energy stored in the capacitor change? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी संधारित्र की धारिता दोगुनी कर दी जाती है, जबकि उसके सिरों पर विभवांतर उसके प्रारंभिक मान का आधा कर दिया जाता है। संधारित्र में संचित ऊर्जा किस गुणक से बदलती है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)</b><br>\\(U = \\frac{1}{2}CV^2\\)<br>\\(U' = \\frac{1}{2}(2C)\\left(\\frac{V}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{2}CV^2 \\times \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{U}{2}\\)<br>The energy becomes <b><u>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)</u></b> of its initial value.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Energy stored in a capacitor: \\(U = \\frac{1}{2}CV^2 = \\frac{Q^2}{2C} = \\frac{1}{2}QV\\).<br>• SI unit of capacitance is the <b>farad (F)</b>; \\(C = \\frac{Q}{V}\\).<br>• Capacitors in parallel: \\(C = C_1 + C_2\\); in series: \\(\\frac{1}{C} = \\frac{1}{C_1} + \\frac{1}{C_2}\\).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)</b><br>\\(U = \\frac{1}{2}CV^2\\)<br>\\(U' = \\frac{1}{2}(2C)\\left(\\frac{V}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{2}CV^2 \\times \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{U}{2}\\)<br>ऊर्जा अपने प्रारंभिक मान की <b><u>\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)</u></b> हो जाती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• संधारित्र में संचित ऊर्जा: \\(U = \\frac{1}{2}CV^2 = \\frac{Q^2}{2C} = \\frac{1}{2}QV\\)।<br>• धारिता (Capacitance) का SI मात्रक <b>फैराड (F)</b> है; \\(C = \\frac{Q}{V}\\)।<br>• समांतर क्रम में: \\(C = C_1 + C_2\\); श्रेणी क्रम में: \\(\\frac{1}{C} = \\frac{1}{C_1} + \\frac{1}{C_2}\\)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000072128","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"The economic liberalisation reforms in India were introduced during which Five-Year Plan? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में आर्थिक उदारीकरण सुधार किस पंचवर्षीय योजना के दौरान शुरू किए गए? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Seventh Five-Year Plan","hi":"सातवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना"},"2":{"en":"Eighth Five-Year Plan","hi":"आठवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना"},"3":{"en":"Ninth Five-Year Plan","hi":"नौवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना"},"4":{"en":"Tenth Five-Year Plan","hi":"दसवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Eighth Five-Year Plan</b><br>The LPG reforms began in <b>1991</b>, and the <b><u>Eighth Five-Year Plan (1992–97)</u></b> was the first plan launched after liberalisation; it was framed to support the reforms.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• 1990–92 had <b>Annual Plans</b> due to political instability; the Eighth Plan began on <b>1 April 1992</b>.<br>• The Eighth Plan's focus was <b>human resource development</b>; it is linked to the <b>Rao–Manmohan model</b>.<br>• It achieved growth of about <b>6.8%</b> against a target of 5.6%.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – आठवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना</b><br>LPG सुधार <b>1991</b> में शुरू हुए और <b><u>आठवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना (1992–97)</u></b> उदारीकरण के बाद शुरू की गई पहली योजना थी, जिसे सुधारों के अनुरूप बनाया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• राजनीतिक अस्थिरता के कारण 1990–92 में <b>वार्षिक योजनाएँ</b> रहीं; आठवीं योजना <b>1 अप्रैल 1992</b> से शुरू हुई।<br>• आठवीं योजना का मुख्य फोकस <b>मानव संसाधन विकास</b> था; इसे <b>राव–मनमोहन मॉडल</b> से जोड़ा जाता है।<br>• इसने 5.6% लक्ष्य के मुकाबले लगभग <b>6.8%</b> वृद्धि प्राप्त की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000072129","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Governor-General and Viceroy","question":{"en":"During whose viceroyalty was the portfolio system introduced in British India? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ब्रिटिश भारत में विभागीय (पोर्टफोलियो) प्रणाली किसके वायसराय काल में शुरू की गई? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lord Canning","hi":"लॉर्ड कैनिंग"},"2":{"en":"Lord Mayo","hi":"लॉर्ड मेयो"},"3":{"en":"Lord Ripon","hi":"लॉर्ड रिपन"},"4":{"en":"Lord Curzon","hi":"लॉर्ड कर्ज़न"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Lord Canning</b><br>The <b>Indian Councils Act, 1861</b>, passed during <b><u>Lord Canning</u></b>'s viceroyalty, gave legal recognition to the <b>portfolio system</b> introduced by Canning in 1859, under which each member of the council headed a department.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Canning was the <b>first Viceroy of India</b> (1858) after the Government of India Act, 1858.<br>• <b>Lord Mayo</b> – financial decentralisation (1870); first census attempt (1872).<br>• <b>Lord Curzon</b> – Partition of Bengal (1905).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – लॉर्ड कैनिंग</b><br><b><u>लॉर्ड कैनिंग</u></b> के वायसराय काल में पारित <b>भारतीय परिषद अधिनियम, 1861</b> ने कैनिंग द्वारा 1859 में शुरू की गई <b>पोर्टफोलियो प्रणाली</b> को कानूनी मान्यता दी, जिसमें परिषद का प्रत्येक सदस्य एक विभाग का प्रमुख होता था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत सरकार अधिनियम, 1858 के बाद कैनिंग <b>भारत के पहले वायसराय</b> (1858) बने।<br>• <b>लॉर्ड मेयो</b> – वित्तीय विकेंद्रीकरण (1870); पहला जनगणना प्रयास (1872)।<br>• <b>लॉर्ड कर्ज़न</b> – बंगाल विभाजन (1905)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000072130","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Digestion and Respiration","question":{"en":"A student repeatedly lifts a 5-kilogram bag and experiences muscle fatigue during the activity. Which substance is traditionally described as accumulating in the muscles when the oxygen supply is insufficient? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक छात्र बार-बार 5 किलोग्राम का बैग उठाता है और इस गतिविधि के दौरान मांसपेशियों में थकान महसूस करता है। ऑक्सीजन की आपूर्ति अपर्याप्त होने पर पारंपरिक रूप से किस पदार्थ के मांसपेशियों में जमा होने का वर्णन किया जाता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Glucose","hi":"ग्लूकोज़"},"2":{"en":"Lactic acid","hi":"लैक्टिक अम्ल"},"3":{"en":"Chlorophyll","hi":"क्लोरोफिल"},"4":{"en":"Hemoglobin","hi":"हीमोग्लोबिन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Lactic acid</b><br>During heavy exercise, oxygen supply falls short and muscle cells carry out <b>anaerobic respiration</b>, converting pyruvate into <b><u>lactic acid</u></b>. Its build-up causes muscle cramps and fatigue.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In muscles: Glucose → Pyruvate → <b>Lactic acid + energy</b> (no oxygen).<br>• In yeast: Glucose → <b>Ethanol + CO₂</b> (fermentation).<br>• Aerobic respiration in <b>mitochondria</b> gives CO₂, water and much more energy (ATP).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – लैक्टिक अम्ल</b><br>भारी व्यायाम के दौरान ऑक्सीजन की आपूर्ति कम पड़ती है और मांसपेशी कोशिकाएँ <b>अवायवीय श्वसन (Anaerobic respiration)</b> करती हैं, जिसमें पाइरुवेट <b><u>लैक्टिक अम्ल (Lactic acid)</u></b> में बदलता है। इसके जमाव से ऐंठन और थकान होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मांसपेशियों में: ग्लूकोज़ → पाइरुवेट → <b>लैक्टिक अम्ल + ऊर्जा</b> (ऑक्सीजन के बिना)।<br>• यीस्ट में: ग्लूकोज़ → <b>एथेनॉल + CO₂</b> (किण्वन – Fermentation)।<br>• <b>माइटोकॉन्ड्रिया</b> में वायवीय श्वसन से CO₂, जल और बहुत अधिक ऊर्जा (ATP) मिलती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000072131","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A right prism has a hexagonal base with an area of 90 cm². The height of the prism is 20 cm. Find the volume. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक लंब प्रिज़्म का आधार षट्भुज है जिसका क्षेत्रफल 90 cm² है। प्रिज़्म की ऊँचाई 20 cm है। आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1800 cm³"},"2":{"en":"2000 cm³"},"3":{"en":"2200 cm³"},"4":{"en":"2500 cm³"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Volume of a prism \\(=\\) base area \\(\\times\\) height<br>\\(= 90 \\times 20\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1800\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1800 cm³.</b>","hi":"प्रिज़्म का आयतन \\(=\\) आधार क्षेत्रफल \\(\\times\\) ऊँचाई<br>\\(= 90 \\times 20\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1800\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1800 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000072132","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"What is the ratio of the sum of interior angles of a regular 7-sided polygon (heptagon) to that of a regular 9-sided polygon (nonagon)? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक सम 7-भुजीय बहुभुज (सप्तभुज) और एक सम 9-भुजीय बहुभुज (नवभुज) के अंतःकोणों के योग का अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 : 7"},"2":{"en":"6 : 7"},"3":{"en":"5 : 8"},"4":{"en":"8 : 5"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Sum of interior angles \\(= (n - 2) \\times 180°\\)<br>Heptagon \\(= 5 \\times 180°\\), nonagon \\(= 7 \\times 180°\\)<br>Ratio \\(= 5 : 7 = \\boxed{5 : 7}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 5 : 7.</b>","hi":"अंतःकोणों का योग \\(= (n - 2) \\times 180°\\)<br>सप्तभुज \\(= 5 \\times 180°\\), नवभुज \\(= 7 \\times 180°\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= 5 : 7 = \\boxed{5 : 7}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 5 : 7 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000072133","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A man observes the top of a tower at an angle of elevation of 60°. After moving 10 meters away from the tower in a straight line, the angle of elevation to the top of the tower reduces to 30°. What is the height of the tower? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति एक मीनार के शिखर का उन्नयन कोण 60° देखता है। मीनार से 10 मीटर सीधी दूरी पर दूर जाने पर मीनार के शिखर का उन्नयन कोण घटकर 30° हो जाता है। मीनार की ऊँचाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(5\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(7\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(11\\sqrt{3}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let the height be \\(h\\) and the nearer distance be \\(x\\)<br>\\(\\tan 60° = \\frac{h}{x} \\Rightarrow h = x\\sqrt{3}\\) and \\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{h}{x + 10}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{x\\sqrt{3}}{x + 10} \\Rightarrow x + 10 = 3x \\Rightarrow x = 5\\)<br>\\(h = 5\\sqrt{3}\\) m \\(= \\boxed{5\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(5\\sqrt{3}\\).</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए ऊँचाई \\(h\\) और निकट की दूरी \\(x\\) है<br>\\(\\tan 60° = \\frac{h}{x} \\Rightarrow h = x\\sqrt{3}\\) तथा \\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{h}{x + 10}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{x\\sqrt{3}}{x + 10} \\Rightarrow x + 10 = 3x \\Rightarrow x = 5\\)<br>\\(h = 5\\sqrt{3}\\) m \\(= \\boxed{5\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(5\\sqrt{3}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000072134","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"The value of \\(\\sqrt{0.16} + \\sqrt{0.81} + \\sqrt{1.69} + \\sqrt{0.0025}\\) is: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{0.16} + \\sqrt{0.81} + \\sqrt{1.69} + \\sqrt{0.0025}\\) का मान है: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1.45"},"2":{"en":"3.25"},"3":{"en":"2.65"},"4":{"en":"4.05"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{0.16} = 0.4\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.81} = 0.9\\), \\(\\sqrt{1.69} = 1.3\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.0025} = 0.05\\)<br>Sum \\(= 0.4 + 0.9 + 1.3 + 0.05\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2.65}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2.65.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{0.16} = 0.4\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.81} = 0.9\\), \\(\\sqrt{1.69} = 1.3\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.0025} = 0.05\\)<br>योग \\(= 0.4 + 0.9 + 1.3 + 0.05\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2.65}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2.65 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000072135","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In △PQR, the medians intersect at centroid G. If the segment PG (from vertex to centroid) is 15 cm, what is the length of segment GD (from centroid to the midpoint of QR)? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"△PQR में माध्यिकाएँ केन्द्रक G पर प्रतिच्छेद करती हैं। यदि खंड PG (शीर्ष से केन्द्रक तक) 15 cm है, तो खंड GD (केन्द्रक से QR के मध्यबिंदु तक) की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 cm"},"2":{"en":"7.5 cm"},"3":{"en":"10 cm"},"4":{"en":"12.1 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(PG : GD = 2 : 1\\)<br>\\(GD = \\frac{PG}{2} = \\frac{15}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{7.5\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 7.5 cm.</b>","hi":"\\(PG : GD = 2 : 1\\)<br>\\(GD = \\frac{PG}{2} = \\frac{15}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{7.5\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 7.5 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000072136","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"Which of the following numbers is divisible by 3? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी संख्या 3 से विभाज्य है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45671"},"2":{"en":"58214"},"3":{"en":"67215"},"4":{"en":"89102"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Digit sums: \\(4+5+6+7+1 = 23\\), \\(5+8+2+1+4 = 20\\), \\(6+7+2+1+5 = 21\\), \\(8+9+1+0+2 = 20\\)<br>Only 21 is a multiple of 3<br>\\(\\boxed{67215}\\) is divisible by 3<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 67215.</b>","hi":"अंकों के योग: \\(4+5+6+7+1 = 23\\), \\(5+8+2+1+4 = 20\\), \\(6+7+2+1+5 = 21\\), \\(8+9+1+0+2 = 20\\)<br>केवल 21, 3 का गुणज है<br>\\(\\boxed{67215}\\), 3 से विभाज्य है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 67215 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000072137","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"A and B began a joint venture by investing ₹20,000 and ₹25,000, respectively. B withdrew after four months, and C came in with an investment of ₹15,000. Four months later, A withdrew, and B re-entered with his former investment. Find the sharing ratio of their profits at the end of one year. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A और B ने क्रमशः ₹20,000 और ₹25,000 निवेश करके एक संयुक्त उद्यम शुरू किया। चार महीने बाद B निकल गया और C ₹15,000 के निवेश से जुड़ गया। चार महीने बाद A निकल गया और B अपने पूर्व निवेश के साथ फिर जुड़ गया। एक वर्ष के अंत में उनके लाभ का अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4 : 8 : 3"},"2":{"en":"4 : 5 : 3"},"3":{"en":"16 : 10 : 3"},"4":{"en":"10 : 12 : 7"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Profit shares are capital × time (in months)<br>A: \\(20{,}000 \\times 8 = 1{,}60{,}000\\); B: \\(25{,}000 \\times 4 + 25{,}000 \\times 4 = 2{,}00{,}000\\); C: \\(15{,}000 \\times 8 = 1{,}20{,}000\\)<br>Ratio \\(= 160 : 200 : 120 = \\boxed{4 : 5 : 3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4 : 5 : 3.</b>","hi":"लाभ के हिस्से पूँजी × समय (महीनों में) के समानुपाती हैं<br>A: \\(20{,}000 \\times 8 = 1{,}60{,}000\\); B: \\(25{,}000 \\times 4 + 25{,}000 \\times 4 = 2{,}00{,}000\\); C: \\(15{,}000 \\times 8 = 1{,}20{,}000\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= 160 : 200 : 120 = \\boxed{4 : 5 : 3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4 : 5 : 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000072138","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A sum of money becomes ₹1,452 in 2 years and ₹1,320 in 1 year. Find the rate of compound interest. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कोई धनराशि 2 वर्षों में ₹1,452 और 1 वर्ष में ₹1,320 हो जाती है। चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज की दर ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12%"},"2":{"en":"10%"},"3":{"en":"5%"},"4":{"en":"8%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Interest for the second year \\(= 1452 - 1320 = 132\\)<br>Rate \\(= \\frac{132}{1320} \\times 100\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 10%.</b>","hi":"दूसरे वर्ष का ब्याज \\(= 1452 - 1320 = 132\\)<br>दर \\(= \\frac{132}{1320} \\times 100\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 10% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000072139","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two regular polygons have a number of sides in the ratio 1 : 4, and the difference between their exterior angles is 9°. What are the numbers of sides of these polygons? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो सम बहुभुजों की भुजाओं की संख्या 1 : 4 के अनुपात में है और उनके बहिष्कोणों का अंतर 9° है। इन बहुभुजों की भुजाओं की संख्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30 sides and 110 sides","hi":"30 भुजाएँ और 110 भुजाएँ"},"2":{"en":"23 sides and 120 sides","hi":"23 भुजाएँ और 120 भुजाएँ"},"3":{"en":"21 sides and 110 sides","hi":"21 भुजाएँ और 110 भुजाएँ"},"4":{"en":"30 sides and 120 sides","hi":"30 भुजाएँ और 120 भुजाएँ"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let the sides be \\(n\\) and \\(4n\\); exterior angles are \\(\\frac{360°}{n}\\) and \\(\\frac{360°}{4n}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{360}{n} - \\frac{90}{n} = 9° \\Rightarrow \\frac{270}{n} = 9 \\Rightarrow n = 30\\)<br>Sides \\(= \\boxed{30\\ \\text{sides and } 120\\ \\text{sides}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 30 sides and 120 sides.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए भुजाएँ \\(n\\) और \\(4n\\) हैं; बहिष्कोण \\(\\frac{360°}{n}\\) और \\(\\frac{360°}{4n}\\) हैं<br>\\(\\frac{360}{n} - \\frac{90}{n} = 9° \\Rightarrow \\frac{270}{n} = 9 \\Rightarrow n = 30\\)<br>भुजाएँ \\(= \\boxed{30\\ \\text{sides and } 120\\ \\text{sides}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 30 भुजाएँ और 120 भुजाएँ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000072140","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A quadrant of a circle has an area of \\(\\frac{121\\pi}{4}\\) cm². Find the radius of the circle. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक वृत्त के चतुर्थांश का क्षेत्रफल \\(\\frac{121\\pi}{4}\\) cm² है। वृत्त की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"13 cm"},"2":{"en":"9 cm"},"3":{"en":"11 cm"},"4":{"en":"7 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Area of a quadrant \\(= \\frac{\\pi r^2}{4} = \\frac{121\\pi}{4}\\)<br>\\(r^2 = 121\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{11\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 11 cm.</b>","hi":"चतुर्थांश का क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{\\pi r^2}{4} = \\frac{121\\pi}{4}\\)<br>\\(r^2 = 121\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{11\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 11 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000072141","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The volume of a cone is 588π cm³ and its height is 7 cm. Find the radius of its base. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक शंकु का आयतन 588π cm³ है और उसकी ऊँचाई 7 cm है। उसके आधार की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(3\\sqrt{7}\\) cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(6\\sqrt{7}\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{7}\\) cm"},"4":{"en":"\\(8\\sqrt{7}\\) cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h = 588\\pi\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{3} r^2 (7) = 588 \\Rightarrow r^2 = 252\\)<br>\\(r = \\sqrt{252} = 6\\sqrt{7}\\) cm \\(= \\boxed{6\\sqrt{7}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(6\\sqrt{7}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h = 588\\pi\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{3} r^2 (7) = 588 \\Rightarrow r^2 = 252\\)<br>\\(r = \\sqrt{252} = 6\\sqrt{7}\\) cm \\(= \\boxed{6\\sqrt{7}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(6\\sqrt{7}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000072142","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"The cost price of two articles, A and B, is in the ratio 4 : 5. Article A is sold at a profit of 20% and Article B is sold at a loss of 10%. If the difference between their selling prices is ₹560, find the total cost price of both articles. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो वस्तुओं A और B के क्रय मूल्य 4 : 5 के अनुपात में हैं। वस्तु A को 20% लाभ पर और वस्तु B को 10% हानि पर बेचा जाता है। यदि उनके विक्रय मूल्यों का अंतर ₹560 है, तो दोनों वस्तुओं का कुल क्रय मूल्य ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹16,500"},"2":{"en":"₹16,800"},"3":{"en":"₹18,200"},"4":{"en":"₹12,700"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let CP be \\(4x\\) and \\(5x\\); SP \\(= 4.8x\\) and \\(4.5x\\)<br>Difference \\(= 4.8x - 4.5x = 0.3x = 560 \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{5600}{3}\\)<br>Total CP \\(= 9x = 9 \\times \\frac{5600}{3} = \\boxed{16{,}800}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹16,800.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए क्रय मूल्य \\(4x\\) और \\(5x\\) हैं; विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 4.8x\\) और \\(4.5x\\)<br>अंतर \\(= 4.8x - 4.5x = 0.3x = 560 \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{5600}{3}\\)<br>कुल क्रय मूल्य \\(= 9x = 9 \\times \\frac{5600}{3} = \\boxed{16{,}800}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹16,800 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000072143","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"If the selling price of an article is tripled, the profit becomes five times the original profit. Find the original profit percentage. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि किसी वस्तु का विक्रय मूल्य तीन गुना कर दिया जाए, तो लाभ मूल लाभ का पाँच गुना हो जाता है। मूल लाभ प्रतिशत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"80%"},"2":{"en":"100%"},"3":{"en":"60%"},"4":{"en":"90%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let CP \\(= c\\) and original profit \\(= p\\), so SP \\(= c + p\\)<br>\\(3(c + p) - c = 5p \\Rightarrow 2c = 2p \\Rightarrow p = c\\)<br>Profit \\(= 100\\%\\) of CP \\(= \\boxed{100\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 100%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए क्रय मूल्य \\(= c\\) और मूल लाभ \\(= p\\), अतः विक्रय मूल्य \\(= c + p\\)<br>\\(3(c + p) - c = 5p \\Rightarrow 2c = 2p \\Rightarrow p = c\\)<br>लाभ क्रय मूल्य का \\(100\\%\\) \\(= \\boxed{100\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 100% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000072144","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A man observes the top of a tower at an angle of 30°. After walking 10 m towards it, the angle becomes 60°. Find the approximate height of the tower. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति एक मीनार के शिखर का उन्नयन कोण 30° देखता है। उसकी ओर 10 m चलने पर कोण 60° हो जाता है। मीनार की अनुमानित ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3.7 m"},"2":{"en":"5.7 m"},"3":{"en":"12.7 m"},"4":{"en":"8.7 m"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan 60° = \\frac{h}{x} \\Rightarrow h = x\\sqrt{3}\\); \\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{h}{x + 10}\\)<br>\\(x + 10 = 3x \\Rightarrow x = 5\\)<br>\\(h = 5\\sqrt{3} = 8.66 \\approx \\boxed{8.7\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8.7 m.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan 60° = \\frac{h}{x} \\Rightarrow h = x\\sqrt{3}\\); \\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{h}{x + 10}\\)<br>\\(x + 10 = 3x \\Rightarrow x = 5\\)<br>\\(h = 5\\sqrt{3} = 8.66 \\approx \\boxed{8.7\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8.7 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000072145","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, the angles are ∠B = 50° and ∠C = 70°, which of the following option is correct? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में कोण ∠B = 50° और ∠C = 70° हैं, निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प सही है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BC < AC"},"2":{"en":"AB < BC"},"3":{"en":"AB < AC"},"4":{"en":"BC > AC"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\angle A = 180° - 50° - 70° = 60°\\)<br>Sides are proportional to opposite angles: \\(\\angle C > \\angle A > \\angle B\\)<br>So \\(AB > BC > AC\\), hence \\(\\boxed{BC > AC}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): BC > AC.</b>","hi":"\\(\\angle A = 180° - 50° - 70° = 60°\\)<br>भुजाएँ सम्मुख कोणों के समानुपाती होती हैं: \\(\\angle C > \\angle A > \\angle B\\)<br>अतः \\(AB > BC > AC\\), इसलिए \\(\\boxed{BC > AC}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): BC > AC है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000072146","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta = p\\), then find the value of \\(\\frac{p^2 + 1}{p^2 - 1}\\). [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta = p\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{p^2 + 1}{p^2 - 1}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"sin θ"},"2":{"en":"cosec θ"},"3":{"en":"tan θ"},"4":{"en":"cot θ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sec\\theta - \\tan\\theta = \\frac{1}{p}\\), so \\(p + \\frac{1}{p} = 2\\sec\\theta\\) and \\(p - \\frac{1}{p} = 2\\tan\\theta\\)<br>\\(\\frac{p^2 + 1}{p^2 - 1} = \\frac{p + 1/p}{p - 1/p} = \\frac{2\\sec\\theta}{2\\tan\\theta} = \\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\text{cosec}\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): cosec θ.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sec\\theta - \\tan\\theta = \\frac{1}{p}\\), अतः \\(p + \\frac{1}{p} = 2\\sec\\theta\\) और \\(p - \\frac{1}{p} = 2\\tan\\theta\\)<br>\\(\\frac{p^2 + 1}{p^2 - 1} = \\frac{p + 1/p}{p - 1/p} = \\frac{2\\sec\\theta}{2\\tan\\theta} = \\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\text{cosec}\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): cosec θ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000072147","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"If the ratio of the volumes of two spheres is 64 : 125, what is the ratio of their total surface areas? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो गोलों के आयतनों का अनुपात 64 : 125 है, तो उनके कुल पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफलों का अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4:5"},"2":{"en":"6:5"},"3":{"en":"11:24"},"4":{"en":"16:25"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Ratio of radii \\(= \\sqrt[3]{64} : \\sqrt[3]{125} = 4 : 5\\)<br>Ratio of surface areas \\(= 4^2 : 5^2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{16 : 25}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 16:25.</b>","hi":"त्रिज्याओं का अनुपात \\(= \\sqrt[3]{64} : \\sqrt[3]{125} = 4 : 5\\)<br>पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफलों का अनुपात \\(= 4^2 : 5^2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{16 : 25}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 16:25 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000072148","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle △ABC, AD and BE are altitudes such that AD ⊥ BC and BE ⊥ AC. The altitudes intersect at point F. If the length of CF is equal to the length of AB, determine the measure of ∠ACB. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"त्रिभुज △ABC में, AD और BE लंब इस प्रकार हैं कि AD ⊥ BC और BE ⊥ AC। लंब बिंदु F पर प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं। यदि CF की लंबाई AB की लंबाई के बराबर है, तो ∠ACB का माप ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30°"},"2":{"en":"45°"},"3":{"en":"60°"},"4":{"en":"75°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"F is the orthocentre; in the right triangles formed, \\(\\triangle ABF\\) and \\(\\triangle CEF\\) give \\(\\angle ABF = \\angle ACF\\)...<br>The standard result is that \\(CF = AB\\) whenever \\(\\angle C = 45°\\) (then the altitude from C equals half of \\(AB/\\ldots\\) in the 45° configuration)<br>\\(\\angle ACB = \\boxed{45°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 45°.</b>","hi":"F लंबकेन्द्र है; बने समकोण त्रिभुजों \\(\\triangle ABF\\) तथा \\(\\triangle CEF\\) से \\(\\angle ABF = \\angle ACF\\) मिलता है<br>मानक परिणाम के अनुसार \\(\\angle C = 45°\\) होने पर \\(CF = AB\\) होता है<br>\\(\\angle ACB = \\boxed{45°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 45° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000072149","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A trader borrowed ₹90,000 at a fixed rate of simple interest. After 5 years, he repaid ₹1,21,500. If he had borrowed ₹1,50,000 at the same rate and for the same period, what would have been the total amount repaid? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक व्यापारी ने एक निश्चित साधारण ब्याज दर पर ₹90,000 उधार लिए। 5 वर्ष बाद उसने ₹1,21,500 चुकाए। यदि उसने उसी दर पर और उसी अवधि के लिए ₹1,50,000 उधार लिए होते, तो कुल कितनी राशि चुकानी पड़ती? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹1,04,500"},"2":{"en":"₹2,02,500"},"3":{"en":"₹2,03,300"},"4":{"en":"₹1,05,900"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Interest paid \\(= 1{,}21{,}500 - 90{,}000 = 31{,}500\\)<br>Rate \\(= \\frac{31{,}500 \\times 100}{90{,}000 \\times 5} = 7\\%\\)<br>New interest \\(= \\frac{1{,}50{,}000 \\times 7 \\times 5}{100} = 52{,}500\\)<br>Amount ₹\\(= 1{,}50{,}000 + 52{,}500 = \\boxed{2{,}02{,}500}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹2,02,500.</b>","hi":"चुकाया गया ब्याज \\(= 1{,}21{,}500 - 90{,}000 = 31{,}500\\)<br>दर \\(= \\frac{31{,}500 \\times 100}{90{,}000 \\times 5} = 7\\%\\)<br>नया ब्याज \\(= \\frac{1{,}50{,}000 \\times 7 \\times 5}{100} = 52{,}500\\)<br>राशि ₹\\(= 1{,}50{,}000 + 52{,}500 = \\boxed{2{,}02{,}500}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹2,02,500 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000072150","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A team of 5 men and 5 women can complete a task in 12 days, while a team of 2 men and 8 women can complete the same task in 15 days. If a team of 10 women starts the work and works for 5 days, how many men must join them so that the remaining work is completed in exactly 5 more days?<br><br>[Assume that each woman works with equal efficiency as the other women and same for the men.] [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"5 पुरुषों और 5 महिलाओं की एक टीम एक कार्य 12 दिनों में पूरा कर सकती है, जबकि 2 पुरुषों और 8 महिलाओं की टीम वही कार्य 15 दिनों में पूरा कर सकती है। यदि 10 महिलाओं की टीम कार्य शुरू करके 5 दिन कार्य करती है, तो शेष कार्य ठीक 5 और दिनों में पूरा करने के लिए कितने पुरुषों को उनके साथ जुड़ना चाहिए?<br><br>[मान लीजिए कि प्रत्येक महिला की कार्यक्षमता अन्य महिलाओं के समान है और पुरुषों के लिए भी वही बात लागू है।] [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8"},"2":{"en":"9"},"3":{"en":"10"},"4":{"en":"12"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Let a man do \\(m\\) and a woman do \\(w\\) units per day<br>\\(5m + 5w = \\frac{1}{12}\\) and \\(2m + 8w = \\frac{1}{15}\\)<br>Solving: \\(m = \\frac{1}{90}\\), \\(w = \\frac{1}{180}\\)<br>Work in 5 days by 10 women \\(= \\frac{50}{180} = \\frac{5}{18}\\), remaining \\(\\frac{13}{18}\\)<br>In 5 days the team must do \\(\\frac{13}{18}\\), i.e. \\(\\frac{13}{90}\\) per day; 10 women give \\(\\frac{5}{90}\\), so men must give \\(\\frac{8}{90}\\)<br>Number of men \\(= \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 8.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए एक पुरुष \\(m\\) और एक महिला \\(w\\) इकाई प्रतिदिन करती है<br>\\(5m + 5w = \\frac{1}{12}\\) और \\(2m + 8w = \\frac{1}{15}\\)<br>हल करने पर: \\(m = \\frac{1}{90}\\), \\(w = \\frac{1}{180}\\)<br>10 महिलाओं द्वारा 5 दिनों में कार्य \\(= \\frac{50}{180} = \\frac{5}{18}\\), शेष \\(\\frac{13}{18}\\)<br>5 दिनों में \\(\\frac{13}{18}\\) करना है, अर्थात् \\(\\frac{13}{90}\\) प्रतिदिन; 10 महिलाएँ \\(\\frac{5}{90}\\) देती हैं, अतः पुरुषों को \\(\\frac{8}{90}\\) देना होगा<br>पुरुषों की संख्या \\(= \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000072151","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"P, Q and R contract to do a job for Rs. 52000. P alone can do it in 10 days, Q in 15 days and R in 30 days. P starts the work alone. After 2 days, Q joins him. After 3 more days, R also joins them. Then the three of them work together till the completion of the job. What should be Q's share of the earnings? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"P, Q और R ने Rs. 52000 में एक कार्य का ठेका लिया। P अकेला उसे 10 दिनों में, Q 15 दिनों में और R 30 दिनों में कर सकता है। P अकेले कार्य शुरू करता है। 2 दिन बाद Q उसके साथ जुड़ जाता है। 3 और दिनों बाद R भी उनके साथ जुड़ जाता है। फिर तीनों कार्य पूरा होने तक साथ कार्य करते हैं। Q को कमाई का कितना हिस्सा मिलना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rs. 12300"},"2":{"en":"Rs. 13500"},"3":{"en":"Rs. 14500"},"4":{"en":"Rs. 15600"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"One day's work: P \\(= \\frac{1}{10}\\), Q \\(= \\frac{1}{15}\\), R \\(= \\frac{1}{30}\\)<br>P alone for 2 days \\(= \\frac{2}{10} = \\frac{1}{5}\\); P + Q for 3 days \\(= 3\\left(\\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>Remaining \\(= 1 - \\frac{1}{5} - \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{3}{10}\\), done by all three in \\(\\frac{3/10}{1/5} = 1.5\\) days<br>Q worked \\(3 + 1.5 = 4.5\\) days, i.e. \\(\\frac{4.5}{15} = \\frac{3}{10}\\) of the work<br>Q's share \\(= \\frac{3}{10} \\times 52{,}000 = \\boxed{\\text{Rs. } 15{,}600}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Rs. 15600.</b>","hi":"एक दिन का कार्य: P \\(= \\frac{1}{10}\\), Q \\(= \\frac{1}{15}\\), R \\(= \\frac{1}{30}\\)<br>P अकेले 2 दिन \\(= \\frac{2}{10} = \\frac{1}{5}\\); P + Q 3 दिन \\(= 3\\left(\\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>शेष \\(= 1 - \\frac{1}{5} - \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{3}{10}\\), जो तीनों मिलकर \\(\\frac{3/10}{1/5} = 1.5\\) दिनों में करते हैं<br>Q ने \\(3 + 1.5 = 4.5\\) दिन कार्य किया, अर्थात् कार्य का \\(\\frac{4.5}{15} = \\frac{3}{10}\\) भाग<br>Q का हिस्सा \\(= \\frac{3}{10} \\times 52{,}000 = \\boxed{\\text{Rs. } 15{,}600}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Rs. 15600 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000072152","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Solve for acute θ: sin θ = cos(θ + 30°) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"न्यून कोण θ के लिए हल कीजिए: sin θ = cos(θ + 30°) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30°"},"2":{"en":"60°"},"3":{"en":"45°"},"4":{"en":"15°"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin\\theta = \\cos(90° - \\theta)\\)<br>\\(90° - \\theta = \\theta + 30° \\Rightarrow 2\\theta = 60°\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{30°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 30°.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin\\theta = \\cos(90° - \\theta)\\)<br>\\(90° - \\theta = \\theta + 30° \\Rightarrow 2\\theta = 60°\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{30°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 30° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000072153","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"What term must be added to the expression 4a² + 20ab to make it a perfect square trinomial? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"व्यंजक 4a² + 20ab में कौन-सा पद जोड़ा जाए कि वह पूर्ण वर्ग त्रिपद बन जाए? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5b²"},"2":{"en":"25b²"},"3":{"en":"10b²"},"4":{"en":"100ab²"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(4a^2 + 20ab + k = (2a + 5b)^2\\)<br>Since \\(2(2a)(5b) = 20ab\\), the missing term is \\((5b)^2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{25b^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 25b².</b>","hi":"\\(4a^2 + 20ab + k = (2a + 5b)^2\\)<br>चूँकि \\(2(2a)(5b) = 20ab\\), अतः अभीष्ट पद \\((5b)^2\\) है<br>\\(= \\boxed{25b^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 25b² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000072154","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If a² + b² = 89 and ab = 20, find the value of |a − b|. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि a² + b² = 89 और ab = 20 है, तो |a − b| का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"5"},"3":{"en":"7"},"4":{"en":"9"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\((a - b)^2 = a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\\)<br>\\(= 89 - 40 = 49\\)<br>\\(|a - b| = \\boxed{7}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 7.</b>","hi":"\\((a - b)^2 = a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\\)<br>\\(= 89 - 40 = 49\\)<br>\\(|a - b| = \\boxed{7}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 7 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000072155","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Simplify the following radical expression completely:<br><br>\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} + 1}{\\sqrt{2} - 1}\\) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित करणी व्यंजक को पूर्ण रूप से सरलीकृत कीजिए:<br><br>\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} + 1}{\\sqrt{2} - 1}\\) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(3 - 2\\sqrt{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(1 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(3 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(4 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Multiply numerator and denominator by \\((\\sqrt{2} + 1)\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{(\\sqrt{2} + 1)^2}{2 - 1} = 2 + 2\\sqrt{2} + 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3 + 2\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(3 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\).</b>","hi":"अंश और हर को \\((\\sqrt{2} + 1)\\) से गुणा कीजिए<br>\\(= \\frac{(\\sqrt{2} + 1)^2}{2 - 1} = 2 + 2\\sqrt{2} + 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3 + 2\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(3 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000072156","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the correct direct speech form of the given sentence?<br><br>The players were asking if their coach would return before the game. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The players, \"Will our coach can return before the game?\""},"2":{"en":"The players said, \"Will our coach return before the game?\""},"3":{"en":"The players, \"Would our coach return before the game?\""},"4":{"en":"The players said, \"Would our coach return before the game?\""}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'asked if' → said + a yes/no question in inverted form; 'would' (past) changes back to 'will'; 'their' → 'our'.</b><br>Direct: The players said, \"<b>Will</b> our coach return before the game?\"<br>Option 1 – reporting verb missing, and 'will … can' uses two modals<br>Option 3 – reporting verb missing, and 'would' not changed to 'will'<br>Option 4 – 'would' not changed to 'will'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The players said, \"Will our coach return before the game?\".</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000072157","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>A groundbreaking medical discovery<br>P. has been developed by scientists<br>Q. using innovative genetic engineering techniques<br>R. paving the way for more effective vaccines<br>S. which enhances the body’s immune response, [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RSPQ"},"2":{"en":"QPSR"},"3":{"en":"QSPR"},"4":{"en":"PSRQ"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: PSRQ</b><br><b>P</b> gives the verb for the subject 'A groundbreaking medical discovery': 'has been developed by scientists'.<br><b>S</b> 'which enhances the body's immune response,' describes the discovery.<br><b>R</b> 'paving the way for more effective vaccines' shows its result.<br><b>Q</b> 'using innovative genetic engineering techniques' tells how these vaccines are made and closes the sentence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): PSRQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000072158","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with appropriate parts of speech.<br><br>Rarely ______ such blatant disregard for protocol, nor ______ it so openly tolerated. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"had one witnessed, was"},"2":{"en":"one had witnessed, was"},"3":{"en":"had one witnessed, were"},"4":{"en":"had witnessed one, were"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A negative adverb (Rarely, Nor) at the start of a clause takes inversion: auxiliary + subject + verb.</b><br>'Rarely had one witnessed…' – auxiliary 'had' before subject 'one'.<br>'nor was it so openly tolerated' – singular 'it' takes 'was', placed before the subject.<br>Correct sentence: Rarely <b>had one witnessed</b> such blatant disregard for protocol, nor <b>was</b> it so openly tolerated.<br>Option 2 – no inversion after 'Rarely'<br>Option 3 – 'were' does not agree with 'it'<br>Option 4 – wrong word order and 'were' with 'it'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): had one witnessed, was.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000072159","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br><br>He didn’t tell me directly, but <b>reading between the lines</b>, I think he is not happy with them. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Understanding the hidden or implied meaning."},"2":{"en":"Taking words literally as they are written."},"3":{"en":"Skipping parts of a text while reading."},"4":{"en":"Guessing randomly without any context."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Read between the lines (छिपा अर्थ समझना) = to understand what is meant but not said directly.</b><br>He did not say it openly, yet the speaker understood his unhappiness.<br>Example: Reading between the lines of her letter, I sensed she was lonely.<br>Taking words literally (शाब्दिक अर्थ लेना) – the opposite<br>Skipping parts of a text (अंश छोड़ना) – literal, unrelated<br>Guessing randomly (अंदाज़ा लगाना) – the idiom uses clues, not random guesses<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Understanding the hidden or implied meaning.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000072160","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br><br>You should write clear so that the reader understands. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"reader"},"2":{"en":"clear"},"3":{"en":"understands"},"4":{"en":"should"}},"answer":"4","solution":{},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000072161","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?</b><br><br>1. Despite their seemingly simple form, jellyfish possess specialized cells called nematocysts that deliver venomous stings to their prey.<br>2. Scientists continue to study jellyfish to understand their unique regenerative abilities and their potential applications in medicine.<br>3. The evolutionary history of jellyfish dates back over 500 million years, making them one of the oldest living creatures on Earth.<br>4. Some species, like the <i>Turritopsis dohrnii</i>, exhibit biological immortality by reverting to their juvenile state after reaching maturity.<br>5. Their ability to thrive in diverse marine environments has made them a key subject of research in evolutionary biology. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4-3-2-1-5"},"2":{"en":"1-3-4-5-2"},"3":{"en":"3-1-5-4-2"},"4":{"en":"2-1-4-3-5"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 3-1-5-4-2</b><br><b>3</b> introduces jellyfish and their long evolutionary history.<br><b>1</b> 'Despite their seemingly simple form' describes their special stinging cells.<br><b>5</b> 'Their ability to thrive…' explains why they are studied in evolutionary biology.<br><b>4</b> 'Some species' gives a striking example – biological immortality.<br><b>2</b> 'Scientists continue to study…' concludes with ongoing research on regeneration.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3-1-5-4-2.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000072162","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word<b>. Peregrinate</b> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Wander"},"2":{"en":"Roam"},"3":{"en":"Stay"},"4":{"en":"Travel"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Peregrinate (भ्रमण करना, यात्रा करना) = to travel or wander from place to place.</b><br><b>Stay (ठहरना)</b> = to remain in one place ✔<br><b>Wander (भटकना)</b> – synonym<br><b>Roam (घूमना)</b> – synonym<br><b>Travel (यात्रा करना)</b> – synonym<br>More antonyms: remain, settle, abide.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Stay.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000072163","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br><b>Giving a false colouring to</b> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Describing something vividly"},"2":{"en":"Misrepresenting the facts"},"3":{"en":"Hiding something completely"},"4":{"en":"Adding visual detail to a scene"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Give a false colouring to (तथ्यों को तोड़-मरोड़ कर पेश करना) = to present facts in a misleading way.</b><br>Example: The report gave a false colouring to the incident to protect the officials.<br>Describing vividly (सजीव वर्णन करना) – describes accurately, not falsely<br>Hiding something completely (पूरी तरह छिपाना) – the facts are shown, but twisted<br>Adding visual detail (दृश्य विवरण जोड़ना) – literal reading of 'colouring'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Misrepresenting the facts.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000072164","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the <b>correct spelling</b> of the ear-nose-throat specialty. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Otorhinolarynology"},"2":{"en":"Otorhinolaryngology"},"3":{"en":"Otorhinolaringology"},"4":{"en":"Otorrhinolaryngology"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Otorhinolaryngology (नाक-कान-गला चिकित्सा विज्ञान) = the branch of medicine dealing with the ear, nose and throat (ENT).</b><br>It joins oto (ear) + rhino (nose) + laryngo (throat) + logy.<br><b>Otorhinolarynology</b> – 'g' missing in 'laryngo'<br><b>Otorhinolaringology</b> – 'i' in place of 'y' in 'laryn-'<br><b>Otorrhinolaryngology</b> – extra 'r' after 'oto'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Otorhinolaryngology.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000072165","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct <b>one-word substitute</b> for: 'A person who flatters for personal gain.' [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Altruist"},"2":{"en":"Protégé"},"3":{"en":"Mentor"},"4":{"en":"Sycophant"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Sycophant (चाटुकार) = a person who flatters important people to gain an advantage.</b><br><b>Altruist (परोपकारी)</b> = a person who selflessly helps others<br><b>Protégé (शिष्य, संरक्षित व्यक्ति)</b> = a person guided and supported by an experienced person<br><b>Mentor (मार्गदर्शक)</b> = an experienced adviser<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Sycophant.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000072166","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct <b>one-word substitute</b> for: 'Pleasure derived from others' misfortune.' [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Antipathy"},"2":{"en":"Schadenfreude"},"3":{"en":"Empathy"},"4":{"en":"Sympathy"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Schadenfreude (दूसरों के दुख पर खुशी) = pleasure felt at another person's misfortune.</b><br><b>Antipathy (घृणा, विरक्ति)</b> = a strong feeling of dislike<br><b>Empathy (समानुभूति)</b> = the ability to share another's feelings<br><b>Sympathy (सहानुभूति)</b> = feeling sorry for someone's trouble<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Schadenfreude.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000072167","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"<b>Select the correct option:</b><br>Not only ___ the funding, but he also offered strategic guidance. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"did he provide"},"2":{"en":"he provided"},"3":{"en":"he did provide"},"4":{"en":"had he provided"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: When 'Not only' begins a sentence, the auxiliary comes before the subject (inversion).</b><br>The second clause is in the simple past ('offered'), so the auxiliary is 'did' + V1.<br>Correct sentence: Not only <b>did he provide</b> the funding, but he also offered strategic guidance.<br>he provided – no inversion<br>he did provide – no inversion (subject before auxiliary)<br>had he provided – past perfect does not match 'offered'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): did he provide.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000072168","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"<b>Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:</b><br>All the equipments (1)/ needed for the installation (2)/ were procured (3)/ well in advance. (4) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'Equipment' is an uncountable noun – it has no plural form and takes a singular verb.</b><br>Part (1) 'equipments' should be 'equipment'; the verb in part (3) then becomes 'was'.<br>Correct sentence: All the <b>equipment</b> needed for the installation was procured well in advance.<br>Parts (2) and (4) are correct; part (3) changes only as a result of the error in part (1).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): (1).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000072169","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"<b>Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:</b><br>Although the results appear encouraging on the surface, (1)/ yet critics remain sceptical of the methods (2)/ employed in gathering and interpreting (3)/ the underlying datasets. (4) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'Although/Though' is not followed by 'yet' or 'but' in the main clause; one conjunction is enough.</b><br>Part (2) begins with 'yet', which must be removed.<br>Correct sentence: Although the results appear encouraging on the surface, <b>critics remain</b> sceptical of the methods employed in gathering and interpreting the underlying datasets.<br>Parts (1), (3) and (4) are correct; 'sceptical of' is the right preposition.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (2).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000072170","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Change the following from active to passive:</b><br>Why did they cancel the meeting? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Why have the meeting was cancelled?"},"2":{"en":"Why was the meeting cancelled?"},"3":{"en":"Why has the meeting been cancelled?"},"4":{"en":"Why is the meeting cancelled?"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple past question (Wh + did + S + V1) → passive: Wh + was/were + object + V3?</b><br>'the meeting' is singular, so 'was'; 'by them' is dropped.<br>Passive: Why <b>was</b> the meeting <b>cancelled</b>?<br>Option 1 – 'have … was' mixes two auxiliaries<br>Option 3 – present perfect passive; the tense changes<br>Option 4 – simple present passive; the tense changes<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Why was the meeting cancelled?.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000072171","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Change the following from active to passive:</b><br>The proposal should not have undergone such sweeping modifications. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Such modifications should not have been undergone by the proposal."},"2":{"en":"The proposal should not be modified so sweepingly."},"3":{"en":"The modifications should not have been swept into the proposal."},"4":{"en":"The proposal should not have been subjected to sweeping modifications."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'should have + V3' → 'should have been + V3'; 'undergo' is expressed in the passive as 'be subjected to'.</b><br>The proposal is the thing that receives the modifications, so it stays the subject with 'have been subjected to'.<br>Passive: The proposal should not <b>have been subjected to</b> sweeping modifications.<br>Option 1 – 'undergone by the proposal' is unnatural; 'undergo' is not used in the passive<br>Option 2 – 'should not be' changes the perfect time to the present<br>Option 3 – 'swept into' changes the meaning<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The proposal should not have been subjected to sweeping modifications.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000072172","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>The principal was angry <b><i>upon the students.</i></b> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"angry by the students"},"2":{"en":"angry with the students"},"3":{"en":"angry over students"},"4":{"en":"angry on students"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'angry with' a person; 'angry at/about' a thing or situation.</b><br>The students are persons, so 'angry with' is correct.<br>Correct sentence: The principal was <b>angry with</b> the students.<br>angry by – 'by' is not used with 'angry'<br>angry over – used for a matter or issue, not persons; article also missing<br>angry on – 'on' is not used with 'angry'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): angry with the students.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000072173","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"<b>A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.</b><br>The captain said that had they practiced more, they might have won the tournament. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“If we practiced more, we might win the tournament,” said the captain."},"2":{"en":"“Had we practiced more, we might have won the tournament,” said the captain."},"3":{"en":"“If only we would practice more, we might win,” said the captain."},"4":{"en":"“Had we been practicing, we might win,” said the captain."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A third conditional (had + V3 … might have + V3) does not change between direct and indirect speech; only pronouns change.</b><br>'they' → 'we' in the direct form; the tenses stay the same.<br>Direct: “<b>Had we practiced more, we might have won</b> the tournament,” said the captain.<br>Option 1 – second conditional; the meaning changes<br>Option 3 – 'If only we would…' turns it into a wish about the future<br>Option 4 – 'might win' does not match the past condition<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): “Had we practiced more, we might have won the tournament,” said the captain.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000072174","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the most appropriate synonym of the underlined word.</b><br><br>There is an <b><u>implicit</u></b> trust between a doctor and their patient. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Stated clearly"},"2":{"en":"Hidden"},"3":{"en":"Unspoken"},"4":{"en":"Confusing"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Implicit (अंतर्निहित, अव्यक्त) = understood without being stated directly.</b><br><b>Unspoken (अनकहा)</b> = understood without being said ✔<br><b>Stated clearly (स्पष्ट रूप से कहा गया)</b> = explicit – antonym<br><b>Hidden (छिपा हुआ)</b> = deliberately kept out of sight – trust here is not concealed<br><b>Confusing (भ्रामक)</b> = unclear – unrelated<br>More synonyms: tacit, implied, understood.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Unspoken.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000072175","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>In the following question, the first and last parts of the sentence (1 and 6) are given. The rest of the sentence is split into four parts and named P, Q, R, and S. These four parts are not given in their proper order. Read the sentence and find out which of the four combinations is correct.</b><br><br><b>1. The fundamental right</b><br>P. which ensures that every citizen<br>Q. is a cornerstone<br>R. to freedom of speech<br>S. of modern democracy<br><b>6.can express their opinions without fear.</b> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RQSP"},"2":{"en":"PQRS"},"3":{"en":"RPSQ"},"4":{"en":"SRQP"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RQSP</b><br><b>R</b> 'to freedom of speech' completes the subject 'The fundamental right'.<br><b>Q</b> 'is a cornerstone' gives the verb.<br><b>S</b> 'of modern democracy' completes 'cornerstone of…'.<br><b>P</b> 'which ensures that every citizen' joins part 6 'can express their opinions without fear'.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): RQSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000072176","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>Hughie Erskine was charming and generous, but had little money and no successful profession. He wished to marry Laura, yet her father insisted that Hughie must first obtain a respectable income. One day, Hughie visited his friend Alan Trevor, a painter who was completing a portrait of an elderly beggar dressed in torn clothes. The model appeared so weak and miserable that Hughie felt immediate sympathy for him.<br>While Alan briefly left the room, Hughie searched his pockets and found a single gold coin. Although he could scarcely afford to lose it, he placed the coin in the beggar’s hand. The old man thanked him with unusual courtesy. Later, Alan informed Hughie that the supposed beggar was Baron Hausberg, one of the wealthiest men in Europe. The baron had deliberately posed as a poor man for the painting.<br>Hughie was deeply embarrassed. He imagined that the millionaire would laugh at his foolish attempt to offer charity. The following morning, however, a representative of the baron arrived with an envelope. It contained a substantial sum of money described as a wedding gift from “an old beggar.”<br>The incident reveals the difference between wealth and generosity. Hughie possessed very little, yet he was prepared to share it without expecting recognition or reward. The baron, though rich, valued the sincerity of the act because it had been performed under the belief that he was helpless. Charity offered for public approval may flatter the giver, but compassion shown in private reveals character.<br><br><br>Why did Laura’s father hesitate to approve her marriage to Hughie? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He doubted Hughie’s ability to remain generous after marriage."},"2":{"en":"He disliked Hughie’s friendship with the painter Alan Trevor."},"3":{"en":"He expected Hughie to establish a respectable source of income."},"4":{"en":"He believed Hughie lacked sufficient affection and concern for Laura."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"He wished to marry Laura, yet her father insisted that Hughie must first obtain a respectable income.\"</i><br>The father's only condition was a respectable income.<br>Option 1 – Hughie's generosity is never doubted<br>Option 2 – the father's view of Alan Trevor is not mentioned<br>Option 4 – Hughie's affection for Laura is never questioned<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): He expected Hughie to establish a respectable source of income.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000072177","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>Hughie Erskine was charming and generous, but had little money and no successful profession. He wished to marry Laura, yet her father insisted that Hughie must first obtain a respectable income. One day, Hughie visited his friend Alan Trevor, a painter who was completing a portrait of an elderly beggar dressed in torn clothes. The model appeared so weak and miserable that Hughie felt immediate sympathy for him.<br>While Alan briefly left the room, Hughie searched his pockets and found a single gold coin. Although he could scarcely afford to lose it, he placed the coin in the beggar’s hand. The old man thanked him with unusual courtesy. Later, Alan informed Hughie that the supposed beggar was Baron Hausberg, one of the wealthiest men in Europe. The baron had deliberately posed as a poor man for the painting.<br>Hughie was deeply embarrassed. He imagined that the millionaire would laugh at his foolish attempt to offer charity. The following morning, however, a representative of the baron arrived with an envelope. It contained a substantial sum of money described as a wedding gift from “an old beggar.”<br>The incident reveals the difference between wealth and generosity. Hughie possessed very little, yet he was prepared to share it without expecting recognition or reward. The baron, though rich, valued the sincerity of the act because it had been performed under the belief that he was helpless. Charity offered for public approval may flatter the giver, but compassion shown in private reveals character.<br><br><br>What prompted Hughie to give the gold coin to the elderly model? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The model’s apparent suffering immediately awakened Hughie’s compassion."},"2":{"en":"The model’s courteous behaviour suggested that he deserved assistance."},"3":{"en":"Alan had asked Hughie to reward the model for posing patiently."},"4":{"en":"The model’s silence made Hughie believe that payment was expected."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<i>\"The model appeared so weak and miserable that Hughie felt immediate sympathy for him.\"</i><br>The model's apparent misery stirred Hughie's sympathy, so he gave the coin.<br>Option 2 – the courtesy came after the gift, as thanks<br>Option 3 – Alan had left the room and asked nothing<br>Option 4 – the model's silence is not mentioned<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The model’s apparent suffering immediately awakened Hughie’s compassion.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000072178","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>Hughie Erskine was charming and generous, but had little money and no successful profession. He wished to marry Laura, yet her father insisted that Hughie must first obtain a respectable income. One day, Hughie visited his friend Alan Trevor, a painter who was completing a portrait of an elderly beggar dressed in torn clothes. The model appeared so weak and miserable that Hughie felt immediate sympathy for him.<br>While Alan briefly left the room, Hughie searched his pockets and found a single gold coin. Although he could scarcely afford to lose it, he placed the coin in the beggar’s hand. The old man thanked him with unusual courtesy. Later, Alan informed Hughie that the supposed beggar was Baron Hausberg, one of the wealthiest men in Europe. The baron had deliberately posed as a poor man for the painting.<br>Hughie was deeply embarrassed. He imagined that the millionaire would laugh at his foolish attempt to offer charity. The following morning, however, a representative of the baron arrived with an envelope. It contained a substantial sum of money described as a wedding gift from “an old beggar.”<br>The incident reveals the difference between wealth and generosity. Hughie possessed very little, yet he was prepared to share it without expecting recognition or reward. The baron, though rich, valued the sincerity of the act because it had been performed under the belief that he was helpless. Charity offered for public approval may flatter the giver, but compassion shown in private reveals character.<br><br><br>Why did Hughie feel embarrassed after learning the model’s true identity? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He feared Alan would accuse him of interrupting the portrait session."},"2":{"en":"He realised that Laura’s father might hear about his impulsive behaviour."},"3":{"en":"He regretted giving away money that he urgently needed for marriage."},"4":{"en":"He thought the wealthy baron might ridicule his misplaced act of charity."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Hughie was deeply embarrassed. He imagined that the millionaire would laugh at his foolish attempt to offer charity.\"</i><br>He feared that the rich baron would laugh at (ridicule) his charity given to the wrong person.<br>Option 1 – Alan's reaction is not the cause<br>Option 2 – Laura's father is not mentioned here<br>Option 3 – regret over the money is not stated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): He thought the wealthy baron might ridicule his misplaced act of charity.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000072179","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>Hughie Erskine was charming and generous, but had little money and no successful profession. He wished to marry Laura, yet her father insisted that Hughie must first obtain a respectable income. One day, Hughie visited his friend Alan Trevor, a painter who was completing a portrait of an elderly beggar dressed in torn clothes. The model appeared so weak and miserable that Hughie felt immediate sympathy for him.<br>While Alan briefly left the room, Hughie searched his pockets and found a single gold coin. Although he could scarcely afford to lose it, he placed the coin in the beggar’s hand. The old man thanked him with unusual courtesy. Later, Alan informed Hughie that the supposed beggar was Baron Hausberg, one of the wealthiest men in Europe. The baron had deliberately posed as a poor man for the painting.<br>Hughie was deeply embarrassed. He imagined that the millionaire would laugh at his foolish attempt to offer charity. The following morning, however, a representative of the baron arrived with an envelope. It contained a substantial sum of money described as a wedding gift from “an old beggar.”<br>The incident reveals the difference between wealth and generosity. Hughie possessed very little, yet he was prepared to share it without expecting recognition or reward. The baron, though rich, valued the sincerity of the act because it had been performed under the belief that he was helpless. Charity offered for public approval may flatter the giver, but compassion shown in private reveals character.<br><br><br>What made Hughie’s gift especially meaningful to Baron Hausberg? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hughie offered it despite knowing that the baron was testing him."},"2":{"en":"Hughie intended it to strengthen his friendship with Alan Trevor."},"3":{"en":"Hughie gave it privately while believing the recipient was helpless."},"4":{"en":"Hughie expected the recipient to repay him after recovering financially."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"The baron, though rich, valued the sincerity of the act because it had been performed under the belief that he was helpless… compassion shown in private reveals character.\"</i><br>The gift was sincere because Hughie gave it privately to someone he thought was helpless.<br>Option 1 – Hughie did not know the baron's identity<br>Option 2 – the friendship with Alan was not his motive<br>Option 4 – he expected no reward or repayment<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Hughie gave it privately while believing the recipient was helpless.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000072180","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>Hughie Erskine was charming and generous, but had little money and no successful profession. He wished to marry Laura, yet her father insisted that Hughie must first obtain a respectable income. One day, Hughie visited his friend Alan Trevor, a painter who was completing a portrait of an elderly beggar dressed in torn clothes. The model appeared so weak and miserable that Hughie felt immediate sympathy for him.<br>While Alan briefly left the room, Hughie searched his pockets and found a single gold coin. Although he could scarcely afford to lose it, he placed the coin in the beggar’s hand. The old man thanked him with unusual courtesy. Later, Alan informed Hughie that the supposed beggar was Baron Hausberg, one of the wealthiest men in Europe. The baron had deliberately posed as a poor man for the painting.<br>Hughie was deeply embarrassed. He imagined that the millionaire would laugh at his foolish attempt to offer charity. The following morning, however, a representative of the baron arrived with an envelope. It contained a substantial sum of money described as a wedding gift from “an old beggar.”<br>The incident reveals the difference between wealth and generosity. Hughie possessed very little, yet he was prepared to share it without expecting recognition or reward. The baron, though rich, valued the sincerity of the act because it had been performed under the belief that he was helpless. Charity offered for public approval may flatter the giver, but compassion shown in private reveals character.<br><br><br>Which inference best explains the contrast between Hughie’s coin and the baron’s wedding gift? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The coin represents financial carelessness, whereas the gift represents calculated generosity."},"2":{"en":"The coin is given in ignorance, whereas the gift is given to display the baron’s wealth."},"3":{"en":"The coin exposes Hughie’s poor judgment, whereas the gift corrects his misunderstanding."},"4":{"en":"The coin reveals generosity through sacrifice, whereas the gift recognises that moral quality."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Hughie possessed very little, yet he was prepared to share it… The baron, though rich, valued the sincerity of the act…\"</i><br>The coin was a sacrifice by a poor man; the baron's gift rewards and recognises that generosity.<br>Option 1 – the passage praises Hughie's act, not calls it careless<br>Option 2 – the baron's gift was sent privately, not to display wealth<br>Option 3 – the passage does not treat the coin as poor judgment<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The coin reveals generosity through sacrifice, whereas the gift recognises that moral quality.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};